window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 14 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000075181","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"A biotechnology firm observed that teams using advanced simulation software completed drug-development projects faster than teams using conventional modeling techniques. The firm concluded that the software itself caused the increase in efficiency.<br>Which of the following, if true, would most weaken the firm's conclusion? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक जैव प्रौद्योगिकी कंपनी ने देखा कि उन्नत सिमुलेशन सॉफ़्टवेयर का उपयोग करने वाली टीमों ने पारंपरिक मॉडलिंग तकनीकों का उपयोग करने वाली टीमों की तुलना में औषधि-विकास परियोजनाएँ अधिक तेज़ी से पूरी कीं। कंपनी ने निष्कर्ष निकाला कि दक्षता में वृद्धि स्वयं सॉफ़्टवेयर के कारण हुई।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा तथ्य, यदि सत्य हो, तो कंपनी के निष्कर्ष को सबसे अधिक कमज़ोर करेगा? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Teams using the software were assigned less complex projects than the other teams.","hi":"सॉफ़्टवेयर का उपयोग करने वाली टीमों को अन्य टीमों की तुलना में कम जटिल परियोजनाएँ सौंपी गई थीं।"},"2":{"en":"Advanced simulation software requires expensive licensing fees.","hi":"उन्नत सिमुलेशन सॉफ़्टवेयर के लिए महँगे लाइसेंस शुल्क लगते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Conventional modeling techniques are still used in several laboratories.","hi":"पारंपरिक मॉडलिंग तकनीकों का उपयोग अभी भी कई प्रयोगशालाओं में होता है।"},"4":{"en":"Employees reported positive experiences while using the software.","hi":"कर्मचारियों ने सॉफ़्टवेयर का उपयोग करते समय सकारात्मक अनुभव बताए।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The conclusion treats the software as the only cause of faster completion<br>If the software teams handled easier projects, then the nature of the work, not the software, explains the speed<br>Cost, continued use elsewhere and positive experiences do not touch the cause-and-effect claim<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Teams using the software were assigned less complex projects than the other teams.</b>","hi":"निष्कर्ष सॉफ़्टवेयर को तेज़ी से पूर्णता का एकमात्र कारण मानता है<br>यदि सॉफ़्टवेयर वाली टीमों को आसान परियोजनाएँ मिलीं, तो तेज़ी का कारण कार्य की प्रकृति है, सॉफ़्टवेयर नहीं<br>लागत, अन्यत्र उपयोग तथा सकारात्मक अनुभव कारण-संबंध को प्रभावित नहीं करते<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): सॉफ़्टवेयर का उपयोग करने वाली टीमों को अन्य टीमों की तुलना में कम जटिल परियोजनाएँ सौंपी गई थीं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000075182","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"A hospital implemented electronic prescription systems and later observed fewer medication errors. Administrators concluded that electronic prescriptions directly reduced such errors.<br>Which of the following, if true, would most strengthen the administrators' conclusion? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक अस्पताल ने इलेक्ट्रॉनिक पर्ची प्रणाली लागू की और बाद में औषधि संबंधी त्रुटियाँ कम देखीं। प्रशासकों ने निष्कर्ष निकाला कि इलेक्ट्रॉनिक पर्चियों ने ऐसी त्रुटियों को सीधे कम किया।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा तथ्य, यदि सत्य हो, तो प्रशासकों के निष्कर्ष को सबसे अधिक मज़बूत करेगा? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Electronic systems automatically flagged harmful drug interactions.","hi":"इलेक्ट्रॉनिक प्रणालियाँ हानिकारक औषधि अंतःक्रियाओं को स्वतः चिह्नित करती थीं।"},"2":{"en":"Several hospitals expanded emergency care facilities recently.","hi":"हाल में कई अस्पतालों ने आपातकालीन देखभाल सुविधाएँ बढ़ाईं।"},"3":{"en":"Medication demand increased during seasonal illness outbreaks.","hi":"मौसमी बीमारी के प्रकोप के दौरान औषधि की माँग बढ़ी।"},"4":{"en":"The hospital changed its medication error reporting policy after the system was installed.","hi":"प्रणाली लगने के बाद अस्पताल ने औषधि त्रुटि रिपोर्टिंग नीति बदल दी।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The conclusion needs a mechanism by which electronic prescriptions themselves prevent errors<br>Automatic flagging of harmful drug interactions is exactly such a mechanism, so it strengthens the claim directly<br>Facility changes and demand show nothing, and a changed reporting policy would weaken the conclusion<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Electronic systems automatically flagged harmful drug interactions.</b>","hi":"निष्कर्ष के लिए ऐसा तंत्र चाहिए जिससे इलेक्ट्रॉनिक पर्चियाँ स्वयं त्रुटियाँ रोकें<br>हानिकारक औषधि अंतःक्रियाओं को स्वतः चिह्नित करना ठीक ऐसा तंत्र है, इसलिए यह निष्कर्ष को सीधे मज़बूत करता है<br>सुविधाओं में बदलाव और माँग कुछ सिद्ध नहीं करते तथा रिपोर्टिंग नीति बदलना निष्कर्ष को कमज़ोर करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): इलेक्ट्रॉनिक प्रणालियाँ हानिकारक औषधि अंतःक्रियाओं को स्वतः चिह्नित करती थीं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000075183","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"A hotel chain introduced mobile room-key access through smartphones and later received higher guest satisfaction ratings. Executives concluded that mobile key access directly improved guest experience.<br>Which of the following, if true, would most strengthen the executives' conclusion? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक होटल शृंखला ने स्मार्टफ़ोन से मोबाइल रूम-की एक्सेस शुरू किया और बाद में अतिथि संतुष्टि रेटिंग अधिक प्राप्त हुई। अधिकारियों ने निष्कर्ष निकाला कि मोबाइल की एक्सेस ने अतिथि अनुभव को सीधे बेहतर किया।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा तथ्य, यदि सत्य हो, तो अधिकारियों के निष्कर्ष को सबसे अधिक मज़बूत करेगा? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Guests using mobile keys reported shorter check-in waiting times.","hi":"मोबाइल की का उपयोग करने वाले अतिथियों ने चेक-इन में कम प्रतीक्षा समय बताया।"},"2":{"en":"Hotel occupancy increased during holiday travel seasons.","hi":"अवकाश यात्रा के मौसम में होटल अधिभोग बढ़ा।"},"3":{"en":"Smartphone usage expanded significantly among business travelers.","hi":"व्यावसायिक यात्रियों में स्मार्टफ़ोन का उपयोग उल्लेखनीय रूप से बढ़ा।"},"4":{"en":"Several hotels upgraded restaurant facilities during the year.","hi":"वर्ष के दौरान कई होटलों ने रेस्टोरेंट सुविधाएँ उन्नत कीं।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A direct link is needed between mobile keys and a better guest experience<br>Shorter check-in waiting for the guests who used mobile keys supplies that link in the guests' own words<br>The other options describe general trends or unrelated facility upgrades<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Guests using mobile keys reported shorter check-in waiting times.</b>","hi":"निष्कर्ष के लिए मोबाइल की और बेहतर अतिथि अनुभव के बीच सीधा संबंध चाहिए<br>मोबाइल की उपयोग करने वाले अतिथियों द्वारा कम प्रतीक्षा समय बताना अतिथियों के ही शब्दों में यह संबंध देता है<br>शेष विकल्प सामान्य प्रवृत्तियाँ या असंबंधित सुविधा-उन्नयन बताते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): मोबाइल की का उपयोग करने वाले अतिथियों ने चेक-इन में कम प्रतीक्षा समय बताया। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000075184","section":"REASONING","topic":"Counting Figures","question":{"en":"How many triangles are there in the given figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई आकृति में कितने त्रिभुज हैं?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The figure has one outer triangle carrying a horizontal line, and inside the middle band an inverted triangle with a small upright triangle<br>Counting separately: 4 small triangles, 3 triangles made of two parts each (the inverted triangle and the two triangles on its sides) and 2 large triangles (the outer one and the one formed by the base and the middle line)<br>Total = 4 + 3 + 2 = 9<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4_opt3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति में एक बाहरी त्रिभुज है जिसके भीतर एक क्षैतिज रेखा है तथा मध्य पट्टी में एक उल्टा त्रिभुज और उसके भीतर छोटा सीधा त्रिभुज है<br>अलग-अलग गिनने पर: 4 छोटे त्रिभुज, दो भागों से बने 3 त्रिभुज (उल्टा त्रिभुज तथा उसके दोनों ओर के त्रिभुज) और 2 बड़े त्रिभुज (बाहरी त्रिभुज तथा आधार और मध्य रेखा से बना त्रिभुज)<br>कुल = 4 + 3 + 2 = 9<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4_opt3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18_opt4.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q4_opt3.jpg"]}},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000075185","section":"REASONING","topic":"Order & Ranking","question":{"en":"In a row of people, Rahul is 11th from the left, and Aman is 10th from the right. After exchanging places, Rahul becomes 25th from the left. Find the total number of people. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"लोगों की एक पंक्ति में राहुल बाएँ से 11वें और अमन दाएँ से 10वें स्थान पर है। स्थान बदलने के बाद राहुल बाएँ से 25वें स्थान पर आ जाता है। पंक्ति में कुल लोगों की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"32"},"2":{"en":"34"},"3":{"en":"36"},"4":{"en":"38"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"After the exchange Rahul stands where Aman stood, so Aman's place was 25th from the left and 10th from the right<br>Total = 25 + 10 − 1 = 34<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 34.</b>","hi":"स्थान बदलने के बाद राहुल वहीं खड़ा है जहाँ अमन था, अतः अमन का स्थान बाएँ से 25वाँ और दाएँ से 10वाँ था<br>कुल = 25 + 10 − 1 = 34<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 34 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000075186","section":"REASONING","topic":"Counting Figures","question":{"en":"How many triangles are formed in the given figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई आकृति में कितने त्रिभुज बनते हैं?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The square is divided by one vertical line, one horizontal line and both diagonals, and a smaller square grid is drawn in each corner<br>The smallest triangles come to 16, joining two of them gives 8 more triangles of medium size and joining four gives 4 large triangles<br>Total = 16 + 8 + 4 = 28<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"वर्ग को एक ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखा, एक क्षैतिज रेखा तथा दोनों विकर्णों से बाँटा गया है और प्रत्येक कोने में छोटे वर्गों का जाल बना है<br>सबसे छोटे त्रिभुज 16 हैं, दो-दो मिलाने पर 8 और मध्यम आकार के त्रिभुज तथा चार मिलाने पर 4 बड़े त्रिभुज बनते हैं<br>कुल = 16 + 8 + 4 = 28<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt4.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6_opt4.jpg"]}},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000075187","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern in fig. (X) by selecting one of the figures from the four alternatives :<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q7.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आकृति (X) का पैटर्न चार विकल्पों में से एक आकृति चुनकर पूरा कीजिए :<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q7.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is a hexagon whose upper half is filled with thick black and white diagonal bands running from the upper left to the lower right, and only the lower-left quarter is blank<br>The blank part must continue the same slanting bands at the same spacing and with the same width, and the bands must meet the edges exactly where the neighbouring bands end<br>Only option 2 continues the diagonal bands in the same direction and spacing, so it completes the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q7_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) एक षट्भुज है जिसका ऊपरी आधा भाग ऊपर-बाएँ से नीचे-दाएँ जाती मोटी काली-सफ़ेद तिरछी पट्टियों से भरा है और केवल नीचे-बायाँ चौथाई भाग खाली है<br>खाली भाग में उसी दिशा, उसी अंतराल और उसी चौड़ाई की तिरछी पट्टियाँ जारी रहनी चाहिए तथा पट्टियाँ किनारों पर ठीक वहीं मिलनी चाहिए जहाँ पड़ोसी पट्टियाँ समाप्त होती हैं<br>केवल विकल्प 2 में तिरछी पट्टियाँ उसी दिशा और अंतराल में जारी रहती हैं, अतः यही पैटर्न पूरा करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q7_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q7.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q7_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q7_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q7_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q7_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q7_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000075188","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 5 Δ 4 = 41 and 7 Δ 3 = 58, then find the value of 9 Δ 2. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 5 Δ 4 = 41 तथा 7 Δ 3 = 58 है, तो 9 Δ 2 का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"97"},"2":{"en":"85"},"3":{"en":"73"},"4":{"en":"92"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Here a Δ b means the sum of the squares of the two numbers<br>5² + 4² = 25 + 16 = 41 ✔ and 7² + 3² = 49 + 9 = 58 ✔<br>So 9² + 2² = 81 + 4 = 85<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 85.</b>","hi":"यहाँ a Δ b का अर्थ दोनों संख्याओं के वर्गों का योग है<br>5² + 4² = 25 + 16 = 41 ✔ तथा 7² + 3² = 49 + 9 = 58 ✔<br>अतः 9² + 2² = 81 + 4 = 85<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 85 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000075189","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Choose the correct sequence of mathematical operators to replace the asterisks (*) in order to make the following expression a valid equation.<br>96 * 6 * 3 * 45 * 3 * 63 [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित व्यंजक को वैध समीकरण बनाने के लिए तारक चिह्न (*) के स्थान पर गणितीय चिह्नों का सही क्रम चुनिए।<br>96 * 6 * 3 * 45 * 3 * 63 [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"÷, ×, +, ÷, ="},"2":{"en":"+, ÷, −, ×, ="},"3":{"en":"×, +, ÷, −, ="},"4":{"en":"÷, ×, −, ×, ="}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Putting ÷, ×, +, ÷, = gives \\(96 \\div 6 \\times 3 + 45 \\div 3 = 63\\)<br>\\(96 \\div 6 = 16\\) and \\(16 \\times 3 = 48\\); \\(45 \\div 3 = 15\\)<br>\\(48 + 15 = 63\\) ✔ so the equation holds<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ÷, ×, +, ÷, =.</b>","hi":"÷, ×, +, ÷, = रखने पर \\(96 \\div 6 \\times 3 + 45 \\div 3 = 63\\) मिलता है<br>\\(96 \\div 6 = 16\\) तथा \\(16 \\times 3 = 48\\); \\(45 \\div 3 = 15\\)<br>\\(48 + 15 = 63\\) ✔ अतः समीकरण सही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ÷, ×, +, ÷, = है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000075190","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>In a T-20 cricket match, the number of runs scored by the Indian team was 212 and out of these, 160 runs were scored by spinners.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. 10% of the Indian team consists of spinners.<br>II. The opening batters were spinners. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ अनुमान दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक टी-20 क्रिकेट मैच में भारतीय टीम ने 212 रन बनाए और इनमें से 160 रन स्पिनरों ने बनाए।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. भारतीय टीम का 10% भाग स्पिनरों का है।<br>II. शुरुआती बल्लेबाज स्पिनर थे। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही अनुमान II निकलता है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement gives runs scored by spinners, not the number of spinners in the team, so nothing about the percentage of players follows<br>It also does not say who opened the batting, so inference II is unsupported<br>Hence neither inference follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन स्पिनरों द्वारा बनाए गए रन बताता है, टीम में स्पिनरों की संख्या नहीं, अतः खिलाड़ियों के प्रतिशत के बारे में कुछ नहीं निकलता<br>यह भी नहीं कहा गया कि पारी किसने शुरू की, अतः अनुमान II भी आधारहीन है<br>इसलिए कोई भी अनुमान नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो अनुमान I और न ही अनुमान II निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000075191","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"After failing an important entrance exam, a student tells themselves, \"I always fail at everything I try. I am never going to succeed in life.\" This specific pattern of negative thinking demonstrates which of the following mental habits? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक महत्वपूर्ण प्रवेश परीक्षा में असफल होने के बाद एक विद्यार्थी स्वयं से कहता है, \"मैं जो भी प्रयास करता हूँ उसमें सदा असफल होता हूँ। मैं जीवन में कभी सफल नहीं होऊँगा।\" सोच का यह विशिष्ट ढंग निम्नलिखित में से किस मानसिक आदत को दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"High emotional regulation, as they are actively assessing their overall life outcomes.","hi":"उच्च भावनात्मक नियमन, क्योंकि वे अपने जीवन के समग्र परिणामों का सक्रिय मूल्यांकन कर रहे हैं।"},"2":{"en":"A cognitive distortion known as overgeneralization, where a single negative event is viewed as a never-ending pattern of defeat.","hi":"संज्ञानात्मक विकृति जिसे अतिसामान्यीकरण कहते हैं, जहाँ एक नकारात्मक घटना को पराजय का अनंत क्रम मान लिया जाता है।"},"3":{"en":"Practical empathy, as they are demonstrating a deep, compassionate understanding of their own failures.","hi":"व्यावहारिक सहानुभूति, क्योंकि वे अपनी असफलताओं की गहरी और करुणापूर्ण समझ दिखा रहे हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Active listening, as they are carefully tuning into their internal emotional thoughts and processing them constructively.","hi":"सक्रिय श्रवण, क्योंकि वे अपने आंतरिक भावनात्मक विचारों को ध्यान से सुनकर रचनात्मक ढंग से संसाधित कर रहे हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"One failed exam is turned into 'I always fail' and 'I will never succeed'<br>Taking a single event as a permanent, universal pattern is exactly overgeneralization<br>The statement shows no regulation, empathy or listening, so it is a cognitive distortion<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A cognitive distortion known as overgeneralization, where a single negative event is viewed as a never-ending pattern of defeat.</b>","hi":"एक परीक्षा में असफल होना 'मैं सदा असफल होता हूँ' और 'मैं कभी सफल नहीं होऊँगा' में बदल दिया गया है<br>एक घटना को स्थायी और सार्वभौमिक पैटर्न मान लेना ही अतिसामान्यीकरण है<br>इस कथन में नियमन, सहानुभूति या श्रवण नहीं है, अतः यह संज्ञानात्मक विकृति है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): संज्ञानात्मक विकृति जिसे अतिसामान्यीकरण कहते हैं, जहाँ एक नकारात्मक घटना को पराजय का अनंत क्रम मान लिया जाता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000075192","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During a department-wide meeting, a colleague receives sole praise from top management for a successful project that was actually a collaborative team effort. You immediately feel a wave of intense resentment.<br>Which of the following actions demonstrates the most emotionally intelligent first step? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"विभाग-व्यापी बैठक के दौरान एक सहकर्मी को एक सफल परियोजना के लिए शीर्ष प्रबंधन से अकेले प्रशंसा मिलती है, जबकि वह वास्तव में सामूहिक टीम प्रयास था। आपको तुरंत तीव्र असंतोष की लहर महसूस होती है।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी कार्रवाई सबसे अधिक भावनात्मक रूप से बुद्धिमान पहला कदम है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Interrupt immediately to publicly correct the manager and demand equal credit.","hi":"तुरंत बीच में बोलकर प्रबंधक को सबके सामने सुधारें और समान श्रेय की माँग करें।"},"2":{"en":"Suppress your irritation entirely, force a smile, and pretend it does not bother you.","hi":"अपनी चिढ़ पूरी तरह दबा दें, जबरन मुस्कुराएँ और दिखाएँ कि इससे आपको कोई फ़र्क नहीं पड़ा।"},"3":{"en":"Pause to process your resentment and its trigger before finding a constructive solution.","hi":"रचनात्मक समाधान खोजने से पहले रुककर अपने असंतोष और उसके कारण को समझें।"},"4":{"en":"Wait until the meeting ends to vent to other teammates about how selfish the colleague is.","hi":"बैठक समाप्त होने तक प्रतीक्षा करें और साथियों के सामने बताएँ कि सहकर्मी कितना स्वार्थी है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Emotional intelligence begins with recognising and understanding one's own emotion before acting<br>Pausing to process the resentment and what triggered it keeps the response calm and allows a constructive solution later<br>Public confrontation, pretence or gossiping all damage relationships, so they are not the right first step<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Pause to process your resentment and its trigger before finding a constructive solution.</b>","hi":"भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता कार्य करने से पहले अपनी भावना को पहचानने और समझने से शुरू होती है<br>असंतोष तथा उसके कारण को समझने के लिए रुकना प्रतिक्रिया को शांत रखता है और बाद में रचनात्मक समाधान देता है<br>सार्वजनिक टकराव, दिखावा या चुगली संबंधों को हानि पहुँचाते हैं, अतः ये सही पहला कदम नहीं हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): रचनात्मक समाधान खोजने से पहले रुककर अपने असंतोष और उसके कारण को समझें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000075193","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"If a mirror is placed on the line XY, which figure will be the mirror image of the question figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि रेखा XY पर दर्पण रखा जाए, तो कौन-सी आकृति प्रश्न आकृति का दर्पण प्रतिबिम्ब होगी?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"As the mirror is vertical, the order of the characters is reversed and every character is flipped left to right<br>The image must therefore start with the mirror of 3 and end with the mirror of g<br>Only option 2 reverses the whole group and correctly mirrors all six characters, so it is the true mirror image<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"चूँकि दर्पण ऊर्ध्वाधर है, अक्षरों/अंकों का क्रम उलट जाता है और प्रत्येक प्रतिबिम्बित होता है<br>अतः प्रतिबिम्ब 3 के दर्पण से आरम्भ होकर g के दर्पण पर समाप्त होना चाहिए<br>केवल विकल्प 2 में पूरा समूह उलटा है और सभी छह अक्षर/अंक सही प्रतिबिम्बित हैं, अतः यही सही दर्पण प्रतिबिम्ब है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000075194","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"The following question consists of four Problem Figures marked A, B, C and D and five Answer Figures marked 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5. Select a figure from amongst the Answer Figures which will continue the series established by the four Problem Figures.<br><b>Problem figures:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q14.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में A, B, C और D से अंकित चार प्रश्न आकृतियाँ तथा 1, 2, 3, 4 और 5 से अंकित पाँच उत्तर आकृतियाँ हैं। उत्तर आकृतियों में से वह आकृति चुनिए जो चारों प्रश्न आकृतियों द्वारा स्थापित श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाएगी।<br><b>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q14.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In the problem figures one short horizontal line is added at the bottom at every step: figure A has only the two vertical lines, B adds one base line, C adds a second and D a third<br>So the next figure must carry four horizontal lines at the bottom with the same two vertical lines<br>Answer figure 2 shows exactly this, while the others change the number of vertical lines or their length<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"प्रश्न आकृतियों में प्रत्येक चरण में नीचे एक छोटी क्षैतिज रेखा जुड़ती है: आकृति A में केवल दो ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखाएँ हैं, B में एक आधार रेखा जुड़ती है, C में दूसरी और D में तीसरी<br>अतः अगली आकृति में उन्हीं दो ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखाओं के साथ नीचे चार क्षैतिज रेखाएँ होनी चाहिए<br>उत्तर आकृति 2 में ठीक यही है, जबकि अन्य विकल्प ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखाओं की संख्या या लंबाई बदल देते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q14.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000075195","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px;text-align:center\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">729</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">81</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">512</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">343</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">49</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">216</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">125</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी प्रकार एक-दूसरे से जुड़े/संबंधित हैं?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px;text-align:center\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">729</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">81</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">512</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">343</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">49</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">216</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">125</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Columns II, III and V","hi":"स्तंभ II, III और V"},"2":{"en":"Columns I, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, III और IV"},"3":{"en":"Columns II, IV and V","hi":"स्तंभ II, IV और V"},"4":{"en":"Columns I, II and V","hi":"स्तंभ I, II और V"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Column II is the cube of column I: 9³ = 729, 8³ = 512, 7³ = 343, 6³ = 216, 5³ = 125<br>Column V is the square of column I: 9² = 81, 8² = 64, 7² = 49, 6² = 36, 5² = 25<br>So columns I, II and V are related to one another<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Columns I, II and V.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ II, स्तंभ I का घन है: 9³ = 729, 8³ = 512, 7³ = 343, 6³ = 216, 5³ = 125<br>स्तंभ V, स्तंभ I का वर्ग है: 9² = 81, 8² = 64, 7² = 49, 6² = 36, 5² = 25<br>अतः स्तंभ I, II और V परस्पर संबंधित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): स्तंभ I, II और V है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000075196","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Select the correct mirror image of the given combination when the mirror is placed at MN as shown.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिखाई गई रेखा MN पर दर्पण रखने पर दिए गए संयोजन का सही दर्पण प्रतिबिम्ब चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"With a vertical mirror the characters appear in the reverse order and each one is flipped left to right<br>The first character of the image must be the mirror of 9 and the last must be the mirror of d<br>Only option 4 keeps both these characters correct along with the middle ones, so it is the correct mirror image<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"ऊर्ध्वाधर दर्पण में अक्षर/अंक उलटे क्रम में और प्रत्येक बाएँ-दाएँ प्रतिबिम्बित होता है<br>प्रतिबिम्ब का पहला अंक 9 का दर्पण और अंतिम अक्षर d का दर्पण होना चाहिए<br>केवल विकल्प 4 में ये दोनों तथा बीच के सभी अंक/अक्षर सही हैं, अतः यही सही दर्पण प्रतिबिम्ब है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16_opt4.jpg"]}},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000075197","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"Carefully observe Figure (X) and identify the option figure in which Figure (X) is embedded exactly as shown.<br>Figure X:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आकृति (X) को ध्यान से देखिए और वह विकल्प आकृति पहचानिए जिसमें आकृति (X) ठीक उसी रूप में अंतर्निहित है।<br>आकृति X:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is a square frame that carries two lines meeting in a V, with a small circle at the meeting point of the lines<br>The answer figure must therefore contain a V of the same width with a small circle sitting at its vertex<br>Only option 4 shows this V with the circle at its vertex in the same shape and position, so figure (X) is embedded there<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) एक वर्गाकार चौखट है जिसके भीतर दो रेखाएँ V रूप में मिलती हैं और रेखाओं के मिलन-बिंदु पर एक छोटा वृत्त है<br>अतः उत्तर आकृति में उसी चौड़ाई का V तथा उसके शीर्ष पर छोटा वृत्त होना चाहिए<br>केवल विकल्प 4 में यह V उसी आकार और स्थिति में वृत्त के साथ है, अतः वहीं आकृति (X) अंतर्निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17_opt4.jpg"]}},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000075198","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In an office of 60 employees, 40 like Tea and 35 like Coffee. Based on this data alone, what are the mathematical minimum and maximum numbers of employees who could like <b>BOTH</b> Tea and Coffee? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"60 कर्मचारियों के एक कार्यालय में 40 को चाय और 35 को कॉफ़ी पसंद है। केवल इसी जानकारी के आधार पर उन कर्मचारियों की गणितीय न्यूनतम और अधिकतम संख्या क्या हो सकती है जिन्हें <b>चाय और कॉफ़ी दोनों</b> पसंद हों? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Minimum: 15, Maximum: 35","hi":"न्यूनतम: 15, अधिकतम: 35"},"2":{"en":"Minimum: 0, Maximum: 35","hi":"न्यूनतम: 0, अधिकतम: 35"},"3":{"en":"Minimum: 15, Maximum: 40","hi":"न्यूनतम: 15, अधिकतम: 40"},"4":{"en":"Minimum: 5, Maximum: 35","hi":"न्यूनतम: 5, अधिकतम: 35"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Minimum = (40 + 35) − 60 = 15, because together the two groups cannot exceed the 60 employees<br>Maximum is limited by the smaller group, which is 35 (all coffee lovers may also like tea)<br>So the range is 15 to 35<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Minimum: 15, Maximum: 35.</b>","hi":"न्यूनतम = (40 + 35) − 60 = 15, क्योंकि दोनों समूह मिलकर 60 कर्मचारियों से अधिक नहीं हो सकते<br>अधिकतम छोटे समूह तक सीमित है, अर्थात 35 (सभी कॉफ़ी प्रेमी चाय भी पसंद कर सकते हैं)<br>अतः परिसर 15 से 35 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): न्यूनतम: 15, अधिकतम: 35 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000075199","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Choose the figure that does NOT follow the same rule.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह आकृति चुनिए जो एक ही नियम का पालन नहीं करती।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In figures (A), (C) and (D) a straight-sided figure is placed inside another straight-sided figure of the same type, with the sides parallel<br>In figure (B) the inner and outer shapes are drops with a curved top, so the shapes have no straight sides at all and the arrangement does not follow the rule<br>Hence figure (B) does not follow the same rule<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृतियों (A), (C) तथा (D) में एक सीधी भुजाओं वाली आकृति उसी प्रकार की दूसरी सीधी भुजाओं वाली आकृति के भीतर समानांतर भुजाओं के साथ रखी है<br>आकृति (B) में भीतरी और बाहरी दोनों आकृतियाँ बूँद के आकार की हैं जिनका ऊपरी भाग वक्र है, अतः इन आकृतियों में सीधी भुजाएँ ही नहीं हैं और यह व्यवस्था नियम का पालन नहीं करती<br>इसलिए आकृति (B) समान नियम का पालन नहीं करती<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q19.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000075200","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Look through all the figures and determine the one that stands out as different.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सभी आकृतियों को देखिए और वह पहचानिए जो भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Figures (A) and (B) are the same shape turned by a quarter turn, and figure (D) is that same shape turned through another quarter turn<br>Figure (C) is not a rotation of this shape; its small rectangle and notch are arranged as a mirror image of the others<br>Hence figure (C) stands out as different<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृतियाँ (A) और (B) एक ही आकृति का चौथाई घुमाव हैं तथा आकृति (D) उसी आकृति का एक और चौथाई घुमाव है<br>आकृति (C) इस आकृति का घुमाव नहीं है; उसमें छोटा आयत और कटाव शेष के दर्पण प्रतिबिम्ब जैसे हैं<br>इसलिए आकृति (C) भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q20.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q16_opt3.jpg"]}},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000075201","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br><b>Question Figures:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। तीसरी और चौथी आकृति के बीच भी वही संबंध स्थापित कीजिए और प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनिए।<br><b>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In (A) → (B) the square with a slanting line inside becomes the same square with a slanting top edge, i.e. the inner line is moved up to become the upper side of the figure<br>Applying the same change to (C), the pentagon with the inner peak becomes the pentagon whose peak is on its upper side, which is answer figure 2<br>Options 1, 4 and 5 change the shape itself instead of moving the inner line<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (A) → (B) में भीतर तिरछी रेखा वाला वर्ग वही वर्ग बन जाता है जिसकी ऊपरी भुजा तिरछी है, अर्थात भीतरी रेखा ऊपर उठकर आकृति की ऊपरी भुजा बन जाती है<br>यही परिवर्तन आकृति (C) पर लगाने से भीतरी शिखर वाला पंचभुज वह पंचभुज बन जाता है जिसका शिखर उसकी ऊपरी भुजा पर है, अर्थात उत्तर आकृति 2<br>विकल्प 1, 4 तथा 5 भीतरी रेखा खिसकाने के बजाय आकृति ही बदल देते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000075202","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"Scenario: In a tense multi-party workplace negotiation, Manager X has maintained a strictly neutral public stance to keep the peace between Team Y and Team Z. However, Manager X privately realizes that Team Z's proposal is objectively more viable. Publicly endorsing Team Z now will cause Team Y to feel betrayed, destroying Manager X's reputation as a fair, unbiased leader.<br>What is the most socially intelligent and logical course of action for Manager X? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"परिदृश्य: एक तनावपूर्ण बहु-पक्षीय कार्यस्थल वार्ता में प्रबंधक X ने टीम Y और टीम Z के बीच शांति बनाए रखने के लिए सार्वजनिक रूप से पूर्ण तटस्थ रुख अपनाया है। परंतु प्रबंधक X निजी तौर पर समझता है कि टीम Z का प्रस्ताव वस्तुनिष्ठ रूप से अधिक व्यवहार्य है। अब सार्वजनिक रूप से टीम Z का समर्थन करने से टीम Y स्वयं को ठगा हुआ महसूस करेगी और निष्पक्ष नेता के रूप में प्रबंधक X की प्रतिष्ठा नष्ट हो जाएगी।<br>प्रबंधक X के लिए सबसे सामाजिक रूप से बुद्धिमान और तार्किक कार्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Endorse Team Z immediately and publicly, prioritizing the objective outcome over Team Y's trust.","hi":"टीम Y के विश्वास की तुलना में वस्तुनिष्ठ परिणाम को प्राथमिकता देते हुए तुरंत सार्वजनिक रूप से टीम Z का समर्थन करें।"},"2":{"en":"Maintain strict public neutrality, even if it results in a deadlocked or suboptimal decision.","hi":"कड़ी सार्वजनिक तटस्थता बनाए रखें, भले ही इससे गतिरोध या अवांछनीय निर्णय हो।"},"3":{"en":"Bridge the gap privately by highlighting shared goals, then propose a unified team solution.","hi":"निजी तौर पर साझा लक्ष्यों को उजागर करके अंतर पाटें और फिर एकीकृत टीम समाधान प्रस्तावित करें।"},"4":{"en":"Inform Team Z privately of the alignment, coaching them to independently outmaneuver Team Y.","hi":"टीम Z को निजी तौर पर इस सहमति की जानकारी दें और उन्हें टीम Y को अलग-थलग करने का प्रशिक्षण दें।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The better proposal must be accepted, but the sense of betrayal in Team Y has to be avoided at the same time<br>Working privately, showing both teams their common goals and then placing a unified solution before everyone keeps the outcome and the relationship intact<br>One-sided endorsement, permanent neutrality or secret coaching all damage either the decision or the trust<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Bridge the gap privately by highlighting shared goals, then propose a unified team solution.</b>","hi":"बेहतर प्रस्ताव स्वीकार होना चाहिए, परंतु साथ ही टीम Y में ठगे जाने की भावना से बचना भी आवश्यक है<br>निजी तौर पर काम करके दोनों टीमों को उनके साझा लक्ष्य दिखाना और फिर सबके सामने एकीकृत समाधान रखना परिणाम तथा संबंध दोनों बनाए रखता है<br>एकपक्षीय समर्थन, स्थायी तटस्थता या गुप्त प्रशिक्षण या तो निर्णय को या विश्वास को हानि पहुँचाते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): निजी तौर पर साझा लक्ष्यों को उजागर करके अंतर पाटें और फिर एकीकृत टीम समाधान प्रस्तावित करें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000075203","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given situation carefully and consider all the relevant facts, conditions and constraints. Choose the option that represents the most appropriate, practical and logical decision based solely on the information provided.<br>A sports academy offers elite badminton scholarships to applicants who are under 16 years of age, have won at least one state-level championship tournament and have maintained a clean disciplinary record. Rohit is 14 years old, has won two state-level championship titles and has never faced any disciplinary issues in his career.<br>What decision should the academy make? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई स्थिति को ध्यान से पढ़िए और सभी प्रासंगिक तथ्यों, शर्तों तथा बाधाओं पर विचार कीजिए। केवल दी गई जानकारी के आधार पर सबसे उपयुक्त, व्यावहारिक और तार्किक निर्णय वाला विकल्प चुनिए।<br>एक खेल अकादमी उन आवेदकों को एलीट बैडमिंटन छात्रवृत्ति देती है जिनकी आयु 16 वर्ष से कम है, जिन्होंने कम से कम एक राज्य-स्तरीय चैंपियनशिप टूर्नामेंट जीता है और जिनका अनुशासनात्मक रिकॉर्ड स्वच्छ रहा है। रोहित 14 वर्ष का है, उसने दो राज्य-स्तरीय चैंपियनशिप खिताब जीते हैं और उसके करियर में कभी कोई अनुशासनात्मक मामला नहीं आया।<br>अकादमी को क्या निर्णय लेना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The candidate should be selected for the elite scholarship.","hi":"अभ्यर्थी को एलीट छात्रवृत्ति के लिए चयनित किया जाए।"},"2":{"en":"The candidate should be rejected for the elite scholarship.","hi":"अभ्यर्थी को एलीट छात्रवृत्ति के लिए अस्वीकार किया जाए।"},"3":{"en":"The application should be referred to the Sports Dean.","hi":"आवेदन खेल डीन को भेजा जाए।"},"4":{"en":"The data provided is inadequate to take a decision.","hi":"निर्णय लेने के लिए दी गई जानकारी अपर्याप्त है।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Age 14 is under 16 ✔, two state-level titles satisfy the championship condition ✔ and the disciplinary record is clean ✔<br>All three conditions are met and no exception is mentioned<br>So the candidate should be selected for the elite scholarship<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The candidate should be selected for the elite scholarship.</b>","hi":"आयु 14 वर्ष, 16 से कम ✔, दो राज्य-स्तरीय खिताब चैंपियनशिप की शर्त पूरी करते हैं ✔ तथा अनुशासनात्मक रिकॉर्ड स्वच्छ है ✔<br>तीनों शर्तें पूरी हैं और कोई अपवाद नहीं दिया गया<br>अतः अभ्यर्थी को एलीट छात्रवृत्ति के लिए चयनित किया जाए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): अभ्यर्थी को एलीट छात्रवृत्ति के लिए चयनित किया जाए। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000075204","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Choose the word from the options that logically completes the given intensity sequence.<br>Newspaper → Section → Column → [?] [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस शब्द को चुनिए जो दिए गए क्रम को तार्किक रूप से पूरा करता है।<br>Newspaper → Section → Column → [?] [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Headline"},"2":{"en":"Article"},"3":{"en":"Edition"},"4":{"en":"Publisher"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The order goes from the whole to its smaller parts: a newspaper has sections, a section has columns<br>A column is written as an article, so article is the next smaller unit<br>Headline comes inside an article, and edition and publisher do not fit this order of parts<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Article.</b>","hi":"क्रम पूर्ण से उसके छोटे भागों की ओर जाता है: समाचार-पत्र में खंड होते हैं और खंड में स्तंभ<br>स्तंभ को लेख के रूप में लिखा जाता है, अतः लेख अगली छोटी इकाई है<br>शीर्षक लेख के भीतर आता है तथा संस्करण और प्रकाशक भागों के इस क्रम में नहीं बैठते<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): Article है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000075205","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"Four different views of a die are shown below. Which symbol appears on the face opposite the \"—\" symbol?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक पासे के चार भिन्न दृश्य नीचे दिखाए गए हैं। \"—\" चिह्न वाले फलक के विपरीत फलक पर कौन-सा चिह्न आता है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"From the four views the symbols seen next to the \"—\" face are ^, # and @<br>Therefore ^, # and @ are all adjacent to \"—\" and cannot be opposite to it<br>The only symbol left is % (written as % over 0), so it lies on the face opposite \"—\"<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"चारों दृश्यों से \"—\" फलक के साथ दिखने वाले चिह्न ^, # तथा @ हैं<br>अतः ^, # और @ सभी \"—\" के आसन्न हैं और उसके विपरीत नहीं हो सकते<br>शेष बचता है केवल % (जो % बटा 0 के रूप में लिखा है), अतः \"—\" के विपरीत फलक पर वही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25_opt4.jpg"]}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000075206","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Himalayas","question":{"en":"Which of the following mountain passes is <b>correctly</b> matched with its respective state? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा पर्वतीय दर्रा अपने संबंधित राज्य के साथ <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bomdi La — Arunachal Pradesh","hi":"बोमडिला — अरुणाचल प्रदेश"},"2":{"en":"Nathu La — Himachal Pradesh","hi":"नाथूला — हिमाचल प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Shipki La — Sikkim","hi":"शिपकी ला — सिक्किम"},"4":{"en":"Lipulekh — West Bengal","hi":"लिपुलेख — पश्चिम बंगाल"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Bomdi La — Arunachal Pradesh</b><br><b>Bomdi La</b> is a mountain pass in the <b>West Kameng district of Arunachal Pradesh</b>, on the route from Tezpur in Assam to Tawang. The other pairs are wrong: Nathu La is in <b>Sikkim</b>, Shipki La in <b>Himachal Pradesh</b> and Lipulekh in <b>Uttarakhand</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Nathu La</b> (4,310 m) is a trade route between Sikkim and the Tibet Autonomous Region, reopened for trade in 2006.<br>• <b>Shipki La</b> connects Kinnaur in Himachal Pradesh with Tibet along the Sutlej gorge, and <b>Lipulekh</b> in Pithoragarh district is one of the routes of the Kailash Mansarovar yatra.<br>• Other important passes are <b>Rohtang and Baralacha La</b> (Himachal), Zoji La and Khardung La (Ladakh) and Jelep La (Sikkim).<br>• Passes in the Himalayas have strategic and trade importance and are used by the Indo-Tibetan Border Police and the army for movement and supply.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – बोमडिला — अरुणाचल प्रदेश</b><br><b>बोमडिला</b> <b>अरुणाचल प्रदेश के पश्चिम कामेंग जिले</b> में स्थित पर्वतीय दर्रा है, जो असम के तेज़पुर से तवांग जाने वाले मार्ग पर है। शेष युग्म गलत हैं: नाथूला <b>सिक्किम</b> में, शिपकी ला <b>हिमाचल प्रदेश</b> में तथा लिपुलेख <b>उत्तराखंड</b> में है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>नाथूला</b> (4,310 मी) सिक्किम व तिब्बत स्वायत्त क्षेत्र के बीच व्यापार मार्ग है, जिसे 2006 में व्यापार हेतु पुनः खोला गया।<br>• <b>शिपकी ला</b> सतलुज गॉर्ज के साथ हिमाचल प्रदेश के किन्नौर को तिब्बत से जोड़ता है, तथा पिथौरागढ़ का <b>लिपुलेख</b> कैलाश मानसरोवर यात्रा के मार्गों में है।<br>• अन्य प्रमुख दर्रे हैं — <b>रोहतांग व बारालाचा ला</b> (हिमाचल), ज़ोजिला व खारदुंग ला (लद्दाख) तथा जेलेप ला (सिक्किम)।<br>• हिमालय के दर्रे सामरिक व व्यापारिक दृष्टि से महत्वपूर्ण हैं और भारत-तिब्बत सीमा पुलिस तथा सेना इनका आवागमन व आपूर्ति हेतु उपयोग करती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000075207","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Electricity","question":{"en":"How many joules (J) are equivalent to 1 kilowatt hour (kWh)? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1 किलोवाट घंटा (kWh) कितने जूल (J) के बराबर होता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3.6 × 10<sup>3</sup> J","hi":"3.6 × 10<sup>3</sup> जूल"},"2":{"en":"3.6 × 10<sup>4</sup> J","hi":"3.6 × 10<sup>4</sup> जूल"},"3":{"en":"3.6 × 10<sup>5</sup> J","hi":"3.6 × 10<sup>5</sup> जूल"},"4":{"en":"3.6 × 10<sup>6</sup> J","hi":"3.6 × 10<sup>6</sup> जूल"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – 3.6 × 10<sup>6</sup> J</b><br>One kilowatt hour equals <b>3.6 × 10<sup>6</sup> joules</b>, because 1 kWh = 1000 W × 3600 s = 3,600,000 J. The kilowatt hour is the commercial unit of electrical energy used in electricity bills.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Energy = power × time, so 1 kW × 1 hour = 1000 watt × 3600 second = <b>3.6 × 10<sup>6</sup> joule</b>.<br>• The joule is the SI unit of energy, and 1 joule = 1 newton-metre; power is measured in watt (1 W = 1 J/s).<br>• The commercial unit of electricity is the kilowatt hour, commonly called \"one unit\" of electricity.<br>• A 100-watt bulb used for 10 hours consumes 1 kWh (1 unit) of energy.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – 3.6 × 10<sup>6</sup> जूल</b><br>एक किलोवाट घंटा <b>3.6 × 10<sup>6</sup> जूल</b> के बराबर होता है, क्योंकि 1 kWh = 1000 वाट × 3600 सेकंड = 3,600,000 जूल। किलोवाट घंटा विद्युत ऊर्जा का वाणिज्यिक मात्रक है, जो बिजली बिल में प्रयुक्त होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ऊर्जा = शक्ति × समय, अतः 1 kW × 1 घंटा = 1000 वाट × 3600 सेकंड = <b>3.6 × 10<sup>6</sup> जूल</b>।<br>• जूल ऊर्जा का SI मात्रक है तथा 1 जूल = 1 न्यूटन-मीटर; शक्ति वाट में मापी जाती है (1 W = 1 J/s)।<br>• विद्युत का वाणिज्यिक मात्रक किलोवाट घंटा है, जिसे सामान्यतः बिजली की \"एक यूनिट\" कहा जाता है।<br>• 100 वाट का बल्ब 10 घंटे जलने पर 1 kWh (1 यूनिट) ऊर्जा खपत करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000075208","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"Which Article of the Indian Constitution provides constitutional protection to the President and Governors from certain court proceedings during their term of office? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का कौन-सा अनुच्छेद राष्ट्रपति तथा राज्यपालों को उनके पदकाल के दौरान कतिपय न्यायालयी कार्यवाहियों से संवैधानिक संरक्षण देता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 359","hi":"अनुच्छेद 359"},"2":{"en":"Article 356","hi":"अनुच्छेद 356"},"3":{"en":"Article 360","hi":"अनुच्छेद 360"},"4":{"en":"Article 361","hi":"अनुच्छेद 361"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Article 361</b><br><b>Article 361</b> protects the <b>President and the Governors</b> from criminal proceedings during their term of office and from arrest or imprisonment, and provides that they shall not be answerable to any court for the exercise of their powers and duties. Civil proceedings for personal acts may be started only after two months’ prior notice.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 356</b> provides for President’s Rule in a state, <b>Article 359</b> deals with the suspension of the enforcement of fundamental rights during an Emergency and <b>Article 360</b> with financial emergency.<br>• The immunity under Article 361 is personal and does not bar judicial review of official acts; the courts can examine the legality of the action even though the President or Governor is not answerable personally.<br>• The conduct of the President cannot be questioned except in an impeachment inquiry, and the protection continues during the term of office.<br>• Governors exercise their powers under Article 161 (pardons) and Article 356 reports, and their immunity is similar to that of the President.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – अनुच्छेद 361</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 361</b> <b>राष्ट्रपति व राज्यपालों</b> को उनके पदकाल में आपराधिक कार्यवाही, गिरफ्तारी या कारावास से संरक्षण देता है तथा निर्धारित करता है कि वे अपनी शक्तियों व कर्तव्यों के प्रयोग हेतु किसी न्यायालय के प्रति उत्तरदायी नहीं होंगे। व्यक्तिगत कार्यों हेतु सिविल कार्यवाही दो माह की पूर्व सूचना पर ही आरंभ हो सकती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 356</b> राज्य में राष्ट्रपति शासन का प्रावधान करता है, <b>अनुच्छेद 359</b> आपातकाल में मूल अधिकारों के प्रवर्तन के निलंबन से तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 360</b> वित्तीय आपातकाल से संबंधित है।<br>• अनुच्छेद 361 का उन्मुक्ति व्यक्तिगत है और यह आधिकारिक कार्यों के न्यायिक पुनर्विलोकन को नहीं रोकती; न्यायालय कार्य की विधिमान्यता की जाँच कर सकते हैं, भले ही राष्ट्रपति या राज्यपाल व्यक्तिगत रूप से उत्तरदायी न हों।<br>• राष्ट्रपति के आचरण पर महाभियोग की जाँच के अतिरिक्त प्रश्न नहीं उठाया जा सकता तथा यह संरक्षण पदकाल तक रहता है।<br>• राज्यपाल अनुच्छेद 161 (क्षमादान) तथा अनुच्छेद 356 की रिपोर्ट के अंतर्गत शक्तियों का प्रयोग करते हैं, और उनकी उन्मुक्ति राष्ट्रपति के समान है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000075209","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Which festival is celebrated in the state of Mizoram? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मिज़ोरम राज्य में कौन-सा उत्सव मनाया जाता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sonam Lochar","hi":"सोनम लोचर"},"2":{"en":"Saga Dawa","hi":"सागा दावा"},"3":{"en":"Hlukhla Kut","hi":"ह्लुखला कुट"},"4":{"en":"Ambubachi","hi":"अम्बुबाची"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Hlukhla Kut</b><br><b>Hlukhla Kut</b> (also written as Hlukhla Kut) is a major harvest festival of <b>Mizoram</b>, celebrated after the harvesting of crops with feasts, dances and traditional songs. Sonam Lochar and Saga Dawa are festivals of Sikkim, and Ambubachi is celebrated at the Kamakhya temple in Assam.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Mizoram’s main festivals are <b>Chapchar Kut, Mim Kut and Pawl Kut</b>, which mark different stages of the agricultural cycle with the Cheraw (bamboo) dance.<br>• <b>Sonam Lochar</b> is the New Year festival of the Tamang community of Sikkim, and <b>Saga Dawa</b> marks the Buddha’s birth, enlightenment and parinirvana.<br>• <b>Ambubachi Mela</b> is held at the Kamakhya Temple in Guwahati, Assam, in the month of Ashadha.<br>• North-Eastern festivals also include <b>Bihu</b> (Assam), Hornbill (Nagaland), Wangala (Meghalaya) and Losar (Arunachal Pradesh).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – ह्लुखला कुट</b><br><b>ह्लुखला कुट</b> <b>मिज़ोरम</b> का प्रमुख फसल उत्सव है, जो फसल कटाई के बाद भोज, नृत्य व पारंपरिक गीतों के साथ मनाया जाता है। सोनम लोचर व सागा दावा सिक्किम के उत्सव हैं, तथा अम्बुबाची असम के कामाख्या मंदिर में मनाई जाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मिज़ोरम के प्रमुख उत्सव <b>चापचार कुट, मिम कुट व पॉल कुट</b> हैं, जो कृषि-चक्र के विभिन्न चरणों को चेराव (बाँस) नृत्य के साथ मनाते हैं।<br>• <b>सोनम लोचर</b> सिक्किम के तमांग समुदाय का नववर्ष उत्सव है, तथा <b>सागा दावा</b> बुद्ध के जन्म, ज्ञान व परिनिर्वाण का स्मरण है।<br>• <b>अम्बुबाची मेला</b> आषाढ़ माह में असम के गुवाहाटी स्थित कामाख्या मंदिर में होता है।<br>• पूर्वोत्तर के अन्य उत्सवों में <b>बिहू</b> (असम), हॉर्नबिल (नागालैंड), वांगला (मेघालय) तथा लोसर (अरुणाचल प्रदेश) सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000075210","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Which of the following pairs of festival and its corresponding state is <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से उत्सव तथा उसके संबंधित राज्य का कौन-सा युग्म <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Padayani Festival – Kerala","hi":"पडयणि उत्सव – केरल"},"2":{"en":"Pooram Festival – Goa","hi":"पूरम उत्सव – गोवा"},"3":{"en":"Sonam Lochar – Manipur","hi":"सोनम लोचर – मणिपुर"},"4":{"en":"Hornbill Festival – Meghalaya","hi":"हॉर्नबिल उत्सव – मेघालय"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Padayani Festival – Kerala</b><br><b>Padayani</b> is a ritual folk art and festival of <b>central Kerala</b>, performed at the Devi temples of Pathanamthitta and Kottayam districts with painted masks and rhythmic steps. The other pairs are wrong: Pooram is a Kerala festival, Sonam Lochar belongs to Sikkim and the Hornbill Festival is held in Nagaland.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Thrissur Pooram</b> is the most famous Pooram festival of Kerala, known for the caparisoned elephants and the percussion ensemble (Panchavadyam).<br>• <b>Hornbill Festival</b> is celebrated every December at Kisama in Nagaland and is called the \"festival of festivals\".<br>• <b>Sonam Lochar</b> is the Tamang New Year of Sikkim; Manipur’s major festivals are Yaoshang, Ningol Chakouba and Lai Haraoba.<br>• Kerala’s other festivals are Onam and Vishu, while Padayani masks are made of areca palm spathes and painted in bright colours.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – पडयणि उत्सव – केरल</b><br><b>पडयणि</b> <b>मध्य केरल</b> की अनुष्ठानिक लोक कला व उत्सव है, जो पथनमथिट्टा व कोट्टयम जिलों के देवी मंदिरों में चित्रित मुखौटों तथा लयबद्ध पदचाल के साथ किया जाता है। शेष युग्म गलत हैं: पूरम केरल का उत्सव है, सोनम लोचर सिक्किम का तथा हॉर्नबिल उत्सव नागालैंड में होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>त्रिशूर पूरम</b> केरल का सर्वाधिक प्रसिद्ध पूरम उत्सव है, जो सजे हाथियों तथा ताल-वाद्य मंडली (पंचवाद्यम) हेतु जाना जाता है।<br>• <b>हॉर्नबिल उत्सव</b> प्रत्येक दिसंबर में नागालैंड के किसामा में मनाया जाता है और इसे \"उत्सवों का उत्सव\" कहा जाता है।<br>• <b>सोनम लोचर</b> सिक्किम के तमांग नववर्ष है; मणिपुर के प्रमुख उत्सव यौशांग, निंगोल चाकौबा व लाई हराओबा हैं।<br>• केरल के अन्य उत्सव ओणम व विशु हैं, तथा पडयणि के मुखौटे सुपारी के पत्तों से बनाकर चमकीले रंगों में चित्रित किए जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000075211","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"As of October <b>2024</b>, Vijaya Kishore Rahatkar heads which statutory body in India? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अक्टूबर <b>2024</b> तक विजया किशोर राहतकर भारत के किस सांविधिक निकाय का नेतृत्व करती हैं? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"National Commission for Protection of Child Rights","hi":"राष्ट्रीय बाल अधिकार संरक्षण आयोग"},"2":{"en":"National Commission for Women","hi":"राष्ट्रीय महिला आयोग"},"3":{"en":"National Commission for Minorities","hi":"राष्ट्रीय अल्पसंख्यक आयोग"},"4":{"en":"Central Social Welfare Board","hi":"केंद्रीय समाज कल्याण बोर्ड"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – National Commission for Women</b><br><b>Vijaya Kishore Rahatkar</b> took charge as the <b>Chairperson of the National Commission for Women</b> in October 2024. She is a former presiding officer of the Maharashtra State Commission for Women and succeeded Rekha Sharma.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The NCW is a <b>statutory body</b> set up in <b>1992</b> under the National Commission for Women Act, 1990, with headquarters at New Delhi.<br>• Its functions include reviewing the constitutional and legal safeguards for women, inquiring into complaints and advising the government on policy.<br>• The National Commission for Protection of Child Rights (NCPCR) was set up in 2007 under the Commissions for Protection of Child Rights Act, 2005, and the National Commission for Minorities in 1992.<br>• The Central Social Welfare Board, established in 1953, is a society that supports voluntary organisations working for women and children.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – राष्ट्रीय महिला आयोग</b><br><b>विजया किशोर राहतकर</b> ने अक्टूबर 2024 में <b>राष्ट्रीय महिला आयोग की अध्यक्ष</b> का पदभार संभाला। वे महाराष्ट्र राज्य महिला आयोग की पूर्व पीठासीन अधिकारी हैं और उन्होंने रेखा शर्मा का स्थान लिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NCW <b>1992</b> में राष्ट्रीय महिला आयोग अधिनियम, 1990 के अंतर्गत गठित <b>सांविधिक निकाय</b> है, जिसका मुख्यालय नई दिल्ली में है।<br>• इसके कार्यों में महिलाओं हेतु संवैधानिक व विधिक सुरक्षाओं की समीक्षा, शिकायतों की जाँच तथा नीति पर सरकार को सलाह सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• राष्ट्रीय बाल अधिकार संरक्षण आयोग (NCPCR) 2007 में बाल अधिकार संरक्षण आयोग अधिनियम, 2005 के अंतर्गत तथा राष्ट्रीय अल्पसंख्यक आयोग 1992 में गठित हुआ।<br>• 1953 में स्थापित केंद्रीय समाज कल्याण बोर्ड एक समिति है, जो महिलाओं व बच्चों हेतु कार्यरत स्वयंसेवी संस्थाओं को सहायता देती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000075212","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"With reference to the Sonam Lochar festival, consider the following statements:<br><b>Statement 1:</b> It is celebrated by the Tamang community.<br><b>Statement 2:</b> It generally occurs during the months of January and February.<br>Which of the statements given above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सोनम लोचर उत्सव के संदर्भ में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br><b>कथन 1:</b> यह तमांग समुदाय द्वारा मनाया जाता है।<br><b>कथन 2:</b> यह सामान्यतः जनवरी व फरवरी माह में होता है।<br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Statement 1","hi":"केवल कथन 1"},"2":{"en":"Only Statement 2","hi":"केवल कथन 2"},"3":{"en":"Both Statement 1 and Statement 2","hi":"कथन 1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither Statement 1 nor Statement 2","hi":"न कथन 1, न ही कथन 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both Statement 1 and Statement 2</b><br>Both statements are correct. <b>Sonam Lochar</b> is the <b>New Year festival of the Tamang community</b> and is generally celebrated in <b>January–February</b> (Magh), mainly in Sikkim, Darjeeling and Nepal, with prayers, feasts and the Damphu dance.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Tamang are one of the major ethnic communities of <b>Sikkim and the Darjeeling hills</b> and follow Tibetan Buddhism; Sonam Lochar marks the beginning of the Tamang year.<br>• The festival is celebrated with <b>ritual offerings at monasteries, the Damphu (drum) dance and community feasts</b>.<br>• Sikkim celebrates <b>Losar</b> (Bhutia New Year), Saga Dawa, Losoong and Pang Lhabsol apart from Sonam Lochar.<br>• Sikkim became a state of India in <b>1975</b> and is the country’s least populous state and first fully organic state.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कथन 1 और 2 दोनों</b><br>दोनों कथन सही हैं। <b>सोनम लोचर</b> <b>तमांग समुदाय का नववर्ष उत्सव</b> है और सामान्यतः <b>जनवरी–फरवरी</b> (माघ) में मनाया जाता है, मुख्यतः सिक्किम, दार्जिलिंग व नेपाल में — प्रार्थनाओं, भोज तथा डम्फु नृत्य के साथ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• तमांग <b>सिक्किम व दार्जिलिंग पहाड़ियों</b> के प्रमुख जातीय समुदायों में हैं और तिब्बती बौद्ध धर्म का पालन करते हैं; सोनम लोचर तमांग वर्ष का आरंभ है।<br>• यह उत्सव <b>मठों में अनुष्ठानिक भेंट, डम्फु (ढोल) नृत्य तथा सामुदायिक भोज</b> के साथ मनाया जाता है।<br>• सिक्किम सोनम लोचर के अतिरिक्त <b>लोसर</b> (भूटिया नववर्ष), सागा दावा, लोसूंग तथा पांग ल्हाबसोल भी मनाता है।<br>• सिक्किम <b>1975</b> में भारत का राज्य बना और यह देश का सबसे कम जनसंख्या वाला तथा पहला पूर्णतः जैविक राज्य है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000075213","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"As of <b>2026</b>, who is serving as India's National Security Advisor (NSA), the principal advisor to the Prime Minister on national security and strategic affairs? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>2026</b> तक राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा तथा सामरिक मामलों में प्रधानमंत्री के प्रमुख सलाहकार, भारत के राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा सलाहकार (NSA) कौन हैं? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ajit Doval","hi":"अजीत डोभाल"},"2":{"en":"Pankaj Saran","hi":"पंकज सरन"},"3":{"en":"Vikram Misri","hi":"विक्रम मिस्री"},"4":{"en":"Rajinder Khanna","hi":"राजिंदर खन्ना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Ajit Doval</b><br><b>Ajit Doval</b> has been serving as India’s <b>National Security Advisor</b> since May 2014 and continues in the post in 2026, having been given an extension. He is a former director of the Intelligence Bureau and was awarded the Kirti Chakra.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The NSA heads the <b>National Security Council</b> and advises the Prime Minister on internal and external security, strategic affairs and intelligence coordination.<br>• The National Security Council, set up in <b>1998</b>, has three tiers — the Strategic Policy Group, the National Security Advisory Board and the National Security Secretariat.<br>• <b>Vikram Misri</b> is the Foreign Secretary, <b>Rajinder Khanna</b> a former NSA (2014–18) and <b>Pankaj Saran</b> a former Deputy NSA.<br>• Ajit Doval is the <b>first NSA to be given a second term</b> and has been associated with the Kashmir policy, counter-terrorism and the Neighbourhood First policy.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अजीत डोभाल</b><br><b>अजीत डोभाल</b> मई 2014 से भारत के <b>राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा सलाहकार</b> हैं और विस्तार के बाद 2026 में भी पद पर हैं। वे आसूचना ब्यूरो के पूर्व निदेशक रहे हैं तथा उन्हें कीर्ति चक्र से सम्मानित किया गया है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NSA <b>राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा परिषद</b> का प्रमुख होता है तथा आंतरिक व बाह्य सुरक्षा, सामरिक मामलों और आसूचना समन्वय पर प्रधानमंत्री को सलाह देता है।<br>• <b>1998</b> में गठित राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा परिषद के तीन स्तर हैं — सामरिक नीति समूह, राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा सलाहकार बोर्ड तथा राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा सचिवालय।<br>• <b>विक्रम मिस्री</b> विदेश सचिव हैं, <b>राजिंदर खन्ना</b> पूर्व NSA (2014–18) तथा <b>पंकज सरन</b> पूर्व उप NSA रहे हैं।<br>• अजीत डोभाल <b>दूसरा कार्यकाल पाने वाले पहले NSA</b> हैं और कश्मीर नीति, आतंकवाद-विरोध तथा पड़ोसी प्रथम नीति से जुड़े रहे हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000075214","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"Under Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation (AMRUT) 2.0, <b>100%</b> water supply coverage is targeted for households in which areas in India? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अटल मिशन फॉर रीजुवेनेशन एंड अर्बन ट्रांसफॉर्मेशन (AMRUT) 2.0 के अंतर्गत भारत में किन क्षेत्रों के घरों हेतु <b>100%</b> जलापूर्ति कवरेज का लक्ष्य है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"All rural households","hi":"सभी ग्रामीण घर"},"2":{"en":"All households in all statutory towns","hi":"सभी सांविधिक नगरों के सभी घर"},"3":{"en":"Only households in Aspirational Districts","hi":"केवल आकांक्षी जिलों के घर"},"4":{"en":"Households in State Capitals only","hi":"केवल राज्य राजधानियों के घर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – All households in all statutory towns</b><br>Under <b>AMRUT 2.0</b>, launched on 1 October 2021, the target is to provide <b>100% water supply coverage to all households in all statutory towns</b>, along with sewerage and septage management, water body rejuvenation and a circular water economy.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• AMRUT 2.0 covers all <b>statutory towns</b> — about 4,800 towns — with an outlay of ₹2.77 lakh crore for 2021–26.<br>• Its goals include <b>universal coverage of water supply and sewerage, recycling of treated water, and reduction of non-revenue water</b> to below 20%.<br>• AMRUT 2.0 is implemented by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, and the rural counterpart for tap water is the <b>Jal Jeevan Mission</b>.<br>• The mission promotes the \"city water balance plan\" and Pey Jal Survekshan to rank cities on water and sanitation performance.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सभी सांविधिक नगरों के सभी घर</b><br>1 अक्टूबर 2021 को शुरू <b>AMRUT 2.0</b> का लक्ष्य <b>सभी सांविधिक नगरों के सभी घरों को 100% जलापूर्ति कवरेज</b> देना है, साथ ही सीवरेज व सेप्टेज प्रबंधन, जल-निकायों का पुनरुद्धार तथा चक्रीय जल अर्थव्यवस्था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• AMRUT 2.0 सभी <b>सांविधिक नगरों</b> — लगभग 4,800 नगर — को 2021–26 हेतु ₹2.77 लाख करोड़ के परिव्यय के साथ समाहित करता है।<br>• इसके लक्ष्यों में <b>जलापूर्ति व सीवरेज की सार्वभौमिक कवरेज, उपचारित जल का पुन:चक्रण तथा गैर-राजस्व जल को 20% से नीचे लाना</b> सम्मिलित है।<br>• AMRUT 2.0 आवास एवं शहरी कार्य मंत्रालय द्वारा क्रियान्वित होता है, तथा नल जल हेतु ग्रामीण समकक्ष <b>जल जीवन मिशन</b> है।<br>• मिशन \"सिटी वाटर बैलेंस प्लान\" तथा पेय जल सर्वेक्षण को बढ़ावा देता है, जो शहरों को जल व स्वच्छता प्रदर्शन पर श्रेणीबद्ध करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000075215","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"Under SISFS (Startup India Seed Fund Scheme) what is the maximum grant a startup can receive for proof of concept or prototype development? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"SISFS (स्टार्टअप इंडिया सीड फंड योजना) के अंतर्गत किसी स्टार्टअप को प्रूफ ऑफ कॉन्सेप्ट अथवा प्रोटोटाइप विकास हेतु अधिकतम कितनी अनुदान राशि मिल सकती है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹30 Lakh","hi":"₹30 लाख"},"2":{"en":"₹20 Lakh","hi":"₹20 लाख"},"3":{"en":"₹40 Lakh","hi":"₹40 लाख"},"4":{"en":"₹1 Crore","hi":"₹1 करोड़"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – ₹20 Lakh</b><br>Under the <b>Startup India Seed Fund Scheme (SISFS)</b>, a recognised startup can receive a grant of up to <b>₹20 lakh</b> for <b>proof of concept, prototype development, product trials and market entry</b>, and up to ₹50 lakh through convertible debentures or debt-linked instruments for commercialisation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• SISFS was launched in <b>2021</b> by the Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT) with a corpus of ₹945 crore for four years.<br>• It is implemented through selected <b>incubators</b>, which disburse the seed fund to eligible startups that are up to two years old at the time of application.<br>• The scheme supports startups working on <b>innovation, scalable technology and impact</b> in areas such as agriculture, health, clean energy and mobility.<br>• Related initiatives are the <b>Fund of Funds for Startups, Startup India Seed Fund, Credit Guarantee Scheme for Startups and BHASKAR</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ₹20 लाख</b><br><b>स्टार्टअप इंडिया सीड फंड योजना (SISFS)</b> के अंतर्गत मान्यता प्राप्त स्टार्टअप को <b>प्रूफ ऑफ कॉन्सेप्ट, प्रोटोटाइप विकास, उत्पाद परीक्षण व बाजार प्रवेश</b> हेतु <b>₹20 लाख</b> तक अनुदान तथा व्यावसायीकरण हेतु परिवर्तनीय डिबेंचर या ऋण-संबद्ध उपकरणों से ₹50 लाख तक सहायता मिल सकती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• SISFS <b>2021</b> में उद्योग संवर्धन एवं आंतरिक व्यापार विभाग (DPIIT) द्वारा चार वर्ष हेतु ₹945 करोड़ के कोष के साथ शुरू की गई।<br>• इसे चयनित <b>इनक्यूबेटरों</b> के माध्यम से क्रियान्वित किया जाता है, जो आवेदन के समय दो वर्ष तक पुराने पात्र स्टार्टअप को बीज निधि वितरित करते हैं।<br>• योजना <b>नवाचार, विस्तारणीय तकनीक व प्रभाव</b> पर कार्यरत स्टार्टअप को कृषि, स्वास्थ्य, स्वच्छ ऊर्जा व गतिशीलता जैसे क्षेत्रों में सहायता देती है।<br>• संबंधित पहलें हैं — <b>स्टार्टअप हेतु फंड ऑफ फंड्स, स्टार्टअप इंडिया सीड फंड, स्टार्टअप हेतु क्रेडिट गारंटी योजना तथा भास्कर</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000075216","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"Which specific metric is used to track progress and ensure accountability for the 100 districts covered under the PM Dhan-Dhaanya Krishi Yojana (PMDDKY) in India? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में पीएम धन-धान्य कृषि योजना (PMDDKY) के अंतर्गत सम्मिलित 100 जिलों की प्रगति दर्ज करने तथा जवाबदेही सुनिश्चित करने हेतु कौन-सा विशिष्ट मापदंड प्रयुक्त होता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Consumer Price Index (CPI)","hi":"उपभोक्ता मूल्य सूचकांक (CPI)"},"2":{"en":"Fiscal Deficit ratio","hi":"राजकोषीय घाटा अनुपात"},"3":{"en":"District-level Key Performance Indicators (KPI)","hi":"जिला-स्तरीय प्रमुख प्रदर्शन संकेतक (KPI)"},"4":{"en":"Gross Domestic Product (GDP) deflator","hi":"सकल घरेलू उत्पाद (GDP) अपस्फीतिकारक"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – District-level Key Performance Indicators (KPI)</b><br>The <b>PM Dhan-Dhaanya Krishi Yojana (PMDDKY)</b>, announced in Budget 2025-26 for <b>100 low-productivity agricultural districts</b>, tracks progress and ensures accountability through <b>district-level Key Performance Indicators</b>, monitored by the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• PMDDKY aims to raise agricultural productivity, improve irrigation and storage, promote crop diversification and enhance the income of small and marginal farmers in the selected districts.<br>• The scheme follows a <b>convergence model</b> with existing schemes such as PM-KISAN, PMFBY, the Agriculture Infrastructure Fund and the Rashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana.<br>• The districts are selected on the basis of <b>low crop intensity, low yield and low credit flow</b>, and the mission is implemented in partnership with state governments.<br>• The Budget also announced a <b>Mission for Aatmanirbharta in Pulses</b> and support for the fisheries and dairy sectors.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जिला-स्तरीय प्रमुख प्रदर्शन संकेतक (KPI)</b><br>बजट 2025-26 में <b>100 कम उत्पादकता वाले कृषि जिलों</b> हेतु घोषित <b>पीएम धन-धान्य कृषि योजना (PMDDKY)</b> प्रगति दर्ज करने तथा जवाबदेही सुनिश्चित करने हेतु <b>जिला-स्तरीय प्रमुख प्रदर्शन संकेतकों</b> का उपयोग करती है, जिनकी निगरानी कृषि एवं किसान कल्याण मंत्रालय करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• PMDDKY का लक्ष्य चयनित जिलों में कृषि उत्पादकता बढ़ाना, सिंचाई व भंडारण सुधारना, फसल विविधीकरण को बढ़ावा देना तथा लघु व सीमांत किसानों की आय बढ़ाना है।<br>• योजना PM-KISAN, PMFBY, कृषि अवसंरचना कोष तथा राष्ट्रीय कृषि विकास योजना जैसी मौजूदा योजनाओं के साथ <b>अभिसरण मॉडल</b> अपनाती है।<br>• जिलों का चयन <b>कम फसल तीव्रता, कम उपज व कम ऋण प्रवाह</b> के आधार पर होता है तथा मिशन राज्य सरकारों के साझेदारी में क्रियान्वित होता है।<br>• बजट में <b>दलहन में आत्मनिर्भरता मिशन</b> तथा मत्स्य व डेयरी क्षेत्र हेतु सहायता की भी घोषणा हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000075217","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: World Map","question":{"en":"Which country hosts Chabahar Port, which has been developed with Indian assistance? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चाबहार बंदरगाह, जिसका विकास भारतीय सहायता से हुआ है, किस देश में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Saudi Arabia","hi":"सऊदी अरब"},"2":{"en":"Oman","hi":"ओमान"},"3":{"en":"United Arab Emirates","hi":"संयुक्त अरब अमीरात"},"4":{"en":"Iran","hi":"ईरान"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Iran</b><br><b>Chabahar Port</b> is located in <b>Iran</b>, on the Gulf of Oman in the Sistan-Baluchestan province, and India has been developing the <b>Shahid Beheshti terminal</b> there through India Ports Global Limited.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chabahar is Iran’s only oceanic port and gives India access to <b>Afghanistan and Central Asia bypassing Pakistan</b>, linking to the International North-South Transport Corridor.<br>• India signed a trilateral agreement with Iran and Afghanistan in <b>2016</b>, and a long-term contract for the Shahid Beheshti terminal was signed in 2024 for ten years.<br>• Chabahar also connects to the <b>Zaranj–Delaram highway</b> in Afghanistan and is important for trade in wheat, pulses and petroleum products.<br>• Other ports of strategic interest to India are <b>Duqm (Oman), Gwadar (Pakistan, developed by China) and Sittwe (Myanmar)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – ईरान</b><br><b>चाबहार बंदरगाह</b> <b>ईरान</b> में सिस्तान-बलूचिस्तान प्रांत में ओमान की खाड़ी पर स्थित है, तथा भारत इंडिया पोर्ट्स ग्लोबल लिमिटेड के माध्यम से वहाँ <b>शाहिद बेहेश्ती टर्मिनल</b> का विकास कर रहा है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• चाबहार ईरान का एकमात्र महासागरीय बंदरगाह है और भारत को <b>पाकिस्तान को दरकिनार करते हुए अफगानिस्तान व मध्य एशिया</b> तक पहुँच देता है, जो अंतर्राष्ट्रीय उत्तर-दक्षिण परिवहन कॉरिडोर से जुड़ता है।<br>• भारत ने <b>2016</b> में ईरान व अफगानिस्तान के साथ त्रिपक्षीय समझौता किया, तथा 2024 में शाहिद बेहेश्ती टर्मिनल हेतु दस वर्ष का दीर्घकालिक अनुबंध हुआ।<br>• चाबहार अफगानिस्तान के <b>जरंज–देलाराम मार्ग</b> से भी जुड़ता है और गेहूँ, दालों व पेट्रोलियम उत्पादों के व्यापार हेतु महत्वपूर्ण है।<br>• भारत की सामरिक रुचि वाले अन्य बंदरगाह हैं — <b>दुक़्म (ओमान), ग्वादर (पाकिस्तान, चीन द्वारा विकसित) तथा सित्त्वे (म्यांमार)</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000075218","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: World Map","question":{"en":"The Andaman and Nicobar Islands are strategically important because they are located close to which major maritime chokepoint? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अंडमान व निकोबार द्वीपसमूह सामरिक दृष्टि से महत्वपूर्ण हैं क्योंकि वे किस प्रमुख समुद्री चोकपॉइंट के निकट स्थित हैं? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Strait of Malacca","hi":"मलक्का जलसंधि"},"2":{"en":"Bosporus Strait","hi":"बोस्पोरस जलसंधि"},"3":{"en":"Suez Canal","hi":"स्वेज नहर"},"4":{"en":"Bab-el-Mandeb Strait","hi":"बाब-एल-मंदेब जलसंधि"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Strait of Malacca</b><br>The Andaman and Nicobar Islands lie at the <b>western entrance of the Strait of Malacca</b>, through which a very large share of world trade and oil passes. This location gives India the ability to monitor the sea lanes between the Indian Ocean and the Pacific, making the islands strategically vital.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Strait of Malacca lies between the Malay Peninsula and Sumatra, and is the shortest sea route between the Indian and Pacific Oceans; about 80% of China’s oil imports pass through it.<br>• India’s <b>Tri-Service Command at Port Blair</b> guards the approaches to the strait, and the islands host INS Baaz at Campbell Bay on Great Nicobar.<br>• The <b>Bosporus</b> is in Turkey, the <b>Suez Canal</b> in Egypt and the <b>Bab-el-Mandeb</b> between Yemen and Djibouti.<br>• The Andaman and Nicobar Islands have an area of about 8,249 sq km, with Port Blair as the capital and Indira Point as India’s southernmost point.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मलक्का जलसंधि</b><br>अंडमान व निकोबार द्वीपसमूह <b>मलक्का जलसंधि के पश्चिमी प्रवेश</b> पर स्थित हैं, जिससे विश्व व्यापार व तेल का बहुत बड़ा भाग गुजरता है। यह स्थिति भारत को हिंद महासागर व प्रशांत महासागर के बीच समुद्री मार्गों पर निगरानी की क्षमता देती है, जिससे ये द्वीप सामरिक दृष्टि से महत्वपूर्ण हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मलक्का जलसंधि मलय प्रायद्वीप व सुमात्रा के बीच है और हिंद व प्रशांत महासागरों के बीच सबसे छोटा समुद्री मार्ग है; चीन का लगभग 80% तेल आयात इससे होकर जाता है।<br>• पोर्ट ब्लेयर में भारत का <b>त्रि-सेना कमान</b> जलसंधि के प्रवेशों की रक्षा करता है, तथा ग्रेट निकोबार में कैंपबेल खाड़ी पर INS बाज़ स्थित है।<br>• <b>बोस्पोरस</b> तुर्की में, <b>स्वेज नहर</b> मिस्र में तथा <b>बाब-एल-मंदेब</b> यमन व जिबूती के बीच है।<br>• अंडमान व निकोबार द्वीपसमूह का क्षेत्रफल लगभग 8,249 वर्ग किमी है, राजधानी पोर्ट ब्लेयर है तथा इंदिरा पॉइंट भारत का दक्षिणतम बिंदु है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000075219","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following best describes the political consequence of the Supreme Court of India's judgment in the Shah Bano case (<b>1985</b>)? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के शाहबानो मामले (<b>1985</b>) के निर्णय के राजनीतिक परिणाम का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन निम्नलिखित में से कौन करता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Strengthening of judicial independence","hi":"न्यायिक स्वतंत्रता का सुदृढ़ीकरण"},"2":{"en":"Weakening of minority identity politics","hi":"अल्पसंख्यक पहचान की राजनीति का कमजोर होना"},"3":{"en":"Electoral backlash leading to legislative reversal of the judgment","hi":"चुनावी प्रतिक्रिया जिसके कारण निर्णय का विधायी उलटाव हुआ"},"4":{"en":"Abolition of criminal maintenance laws","hi":"आपराधिक भरण-पोषण विधियों का उन्मूलन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Electoral backlash leading to legislative reversal of the judgment</b><br>In the <b>Shah Bano case (1985)</b> the Supreme Court upheld the right of a divorced Muslim woman to maintenance under Section 125 CrPC. The judgment provoked a strong political reaction, and the government enacted the <b>Muslim Women (Protection of Rights on Divorce) Act, 1986</b>, which in effect <b>reversed the judgment</b> for Muslim women.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The case arose from a petition by Shah Bano Begum, a 73-year-old divorced woman, against her former husband’s plea that the CrPC did not apply to Muslims.<br>• The judgment led to a national debate on the <b>Uniform Civil Code</b>, and the Supreme Court later reiterated the UCC direction in <b>Sarla Mudgal (1995)</b>.<br>• The 1986 Act restricted maintenance to the iddat period but was later read down by the Supreme Court in <b>Danial Latifi v. Union of India (2001)</b>, which held that reasonable provision must be made.<br>• Maintenance for all women is now governed by Section 144 of the BNSS, 2023, which replaced Section 125 CrPC.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – चुनावी प्रतिक्रिया जिसके कारण निर्णय का विधायी उलटाव हुआ</b><br><b>शाहबानो मामले (1985)</b> में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय ने तलाकशुदा मुस्लिम महिला के भरण-पोषण के अधिकार को CrPC की धारा 125 के अंतर्गत बरकरार रखा। इस निर्णय से तीव्र राजनीतिक प्रतिक्रिया हुई और सरकार ने <b>मुस्लिम महिला (तलाक पर अधिकार संरक्षण) अधिनियम, 1986</b> बनाकर मुस्लिम महिलाओं के लिए निर्णय को <b>व्यावहारिक रूप से उलट दिया</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह मामला 73 वर्षीय तलाकशुदा शाहबानो बेगम की याचिका से उठा, जिसमें पूर्व पति ने कहा था कि CrPC मुस्लिमों पर लागू नहीं होती।<br>• निर्णय से <b>समान नागरिक संहिता</b> पर राष्ट्रीय बहस हुई और सर्वोच्च न्यायालय ने बाद में <b>सरला मुदगल (1995)</b> में UCC का निर्देश दोहराया।<br>• 1986 के अधिनियम ने भरण-पोषण को इद्दत अवधि तक सीमित किया, परंतु सर्वोच्च न्यायालय ने <b>दानियल लतीफी बनाम भारत संघ (2001)</b> में इसे पढ़कर बताया कि उचित प्रावधान आवश्यक है।<br>• अब सभी महिलाओं हेतु भरण-पोषण BNSS, 2023 की धारा 144 से नियंत्रित होता है, जिसने CrPC की धारा 125 का स्थान लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000075220","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"In India, residuary legislative powers are vested in which of the following? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में अवशिष्ट विधायी शक्तियाँ निम्नलिखित में से किसमें निहित हैं? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"President","hi":"राष्ट्रपति"},"2":{"en":"States","hi":"राज्य"},"3":{"en":"Concurrent jurisdiction","hi":"समवर्ती अधिकारक्षेत्र"},"4":{"en":"Parliament","hi":"संसद"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Parliament</b><br>Under <b>Article 248</b> read with entry 97 of the Union List, <b>Parliament has exclusive power to make laws on any matter not enumerated in the State List or the Concurrent List</b> — these are the residuary powers. This follows the Canadian model and gives the Centre a strong position in the federation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Residuary powers in India are with the <b>Union</b>, whereas in the United States and Australia they are with the states.<br>• The <b>Seventh Schedule</b> contains three lists — the Union List (100 subjects), State List (61 subjects) and Concurrent List (52 subjects).<br>• In case of a conflict between Union and state laws on a concurrent subject, the <b>Union law prevails</b> under Article 254, unless the state law has received the President’s assent.<br>• Residuary subjects include matters such as <b>cyber laws, new technologies and taxation of certain services</b> not covered in the three lists.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – संसद</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 248</b> तथा संघ सूची की प्रविष्टि 97 के अनुसार <b>संसद को राज्य सूची या समवर्ती सूची में उल्लिखित न होने वाले किसी विषय पर विधि बनाने की अनन्य शक्ति</b> है — ये अवशिष्ट शक्तियाँ हैं। यह कनाडाई मॉडल का अनुसरण करता है और संघ में केंद्र को मजबूत स्थिति देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में अवशिष्ट शक्तियाँ <b>संघ</b> के पास हैं, जबकि अमेरिका व ऑस्ट्रेलिया में ये राज्यों के पास हैं।<br>• <b>सातवीं अनुसूची</b> में तीन सूचियाँ हैं — संघ सूची (100 विषय), राज्य सूची (61 विषय) तथा समवर्ती सूची (52 विषय)।<br>• समवर्ती विषय पर संघ व राज्य विधियों में टकराव होने पर अनुच्छेद 254 के अंतर्गत <b>संघ की विधि प्रभावी</b> होती है, जब तक राज्य विधि को राष्ट्रपति की स्वीकृति न मिली हो।<br>• अवशिष्ट विषयों में <b>साइबर विधियाँ, नई प्रौद्योगिकियाँ तथा कुछ सेवाओं पर कराधान</b> जैसे विषय आते हैं जो तीन सूचियों में सम्मिलित नहीं हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000075221","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Part 1 and Part 2 of the Constitution","question":{"en":"Under which Article of the Constitution of India does Parliament have the power to alter the name, area, or boundaries of a State? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के संविधान के किस अनुच्छेद के अंतर्गत संसद को किसी राज्य का नाम, क्षेत्र या सीमाएँ बदलने की शक्ति है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 1","hi":"अनुच्छेद 1"},"2":{"en":"Article 2","hi":"अनुच्छेद 2"},"3":{"en":"Article 3","hi":"अनुच्छेद 3"},"4":{"en":"Article 4","hi":"अनुच्छेद 4"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Article 3</b><br><b>Article 3</b> empowers Parliament to make laws for the <b>formation of new states, the alteration of areas, boundaries or names of existing states</b> and the diminution of the area of any state, subject to the requirement of a prior recommendation of the President and reference to the concerned state legislature for its views.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 1</b> declares India, that is Bharat, as a Union of States, and <b>Article 2</b> deals with the admission or establishment of new states.<br>• <b>Article 4</b> provides that laws made under Articles 2 and 3 shall not be deemed to be an amendment of the Constitution under Article 368, so a simple majority suffices.<br>• The views of the state legislature are <b>not binding</b> on Parliament, which was upheld by the Supreme Court in cases relating to the reorganisation of states.<br>• Examples include the <b>Andhra Pradesh Reorganisation Act, 2014</b> (Telangana) and the Jammu and Kashmir Reorganisation Act, 2019.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अनुच्छेद 3</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 3</b> संसद को <b>नए राज्यों के निर्माण, वर्तमान राज्यों के क्षेत्र, सीमाओं या नामों में परिवर्तन</b> तथा किसी राज्य के क्षेत्र में कमी करने की शक्ति देता है, बशर्ते राष्ट्रपति की पूर्व सिफारिश हो तथा संबंधित राज्य विधानमंडल से उसके विचार प्राप्त किए जाएँ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 1</b> भारत को राज्यों के संघ के रूप में घोषित करता है, तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 2</b> नए राज्यों के प्रवेश या स्थापन से संबंधित है।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 4</b> का प्रावधान है कि अनुच्छेद 2 व 3 के अंतर्गत बनी विधियाँ अनुच्छेद 368 के अंतर्गत संविधान का संशोधन नहीं मानी जाएँगी, अतः साधारण बहुमत पर्याप्त है।<br>• राज्य विधानमंडल के विचार संसद पर <b>बाध्यकारी नहीं</b> हैं, जिसे सर्वोच्च न्यायालय ने राज्य पुनर्गठन से संबंधित मामलों में बरकरार रखा।<br>• उदाहरण हैं — <b>आंध्र प्रदेश पुनर्गठन अधिनियम, 2014</b> (तेलंगाना) तथा जम्मू-कश्मीर पुनर्गठन अधिनियम, 2019।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000075222","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who has been appointed as a part-time member of the <b>16<sup>th</sup></b> Finance Commission (XVI FC) of India? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के <b>16वें</b> वित्त आयोग (XVI FC) के अंशकालिक सदस्य के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Arvind Panagariya","hi":"अरविंद पनगढ़िया"},"2":{"en":"Ajay Narayan Jha","hi":"अजय नारायण झा"},"3":{"en":"T. Rabi Sankar","hi":"टी. रवि शंकर"},"4":{"en":"Rajiv Kumar","hi":"राजीव कुमार"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – T. Rabi Sankar</b><br><b>T. Rabi Sankar</b> was appointed as a <b>part-time member of the 16th Finance Commission</b>. He is a former Deputy Governor of the Reserve Bank of India and has expertise in monetary policy, financial markets and payment systems.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 16th Finance Commission was constituted in <b>December 2023</b> under <b>Article 280</b>, with <b>Arvind Panagariya</b> as its Chairman, and submits its report for the award period starting 1 April 2026.<br>• Other members include <b>Ajay Narayan Jha</b> (full-time member) and part-time members such as Annie George Mathew and T. Rabi Sankar.<br>• The Commission recommends the <b>devolution of central taxes to states</b>, grants-in-aid and measures for fiscal discipline; the 15th Finance Commission recommended 41% devolution.<br>• <b>Rajiv Kumar</b> is a former Vice-Chairman of NITI Aayog, not a member of the 16th Finance Commission.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – टी. रवि शंकर</b><br><b>टी. रवि शंकर</b> को <b>16वें वित्त आयोग का अंशकालिक सदस्य</b> नियुक्त किया गया। वे भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक के पूर्व उप-गवर्नर हैं तथा मौद्रिक नीति, वित्तीय बाजार व भुगतान प्रणालियों में विशेषज्ञता रखते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 16वाँ वित्त आयोग <b>दिसंबर 2023</b> में <b>अनुच्छेद 280</b> के अंतर्गत गठित हुआ, जिसके अध्यक्ष <b>अरविंद पनगढ़िया</b> हैं, और इसकी रिपोर्ट 1 अप्रैल 2026 से आरंभ होने वाली अवधि हेतु है।<br>• अन्य सदस्यों में <b>अजय नारायण झा</b> (पूर्णकालिक सदस्य) तथा एनी जॉर्ज मैथ्यू व टी. रवि शंकर जैसे अंशकालिक सदस्य सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• आयोग <b>राज्यों को केंद्रीय करों के हस्तांतरण</b>, सहायता अनुदान तथा राजकोषीय अनुशासन के उपायों की सिफारिश करता है; 15वें वित्त आयोग ने 41% हस्तांतरण की सिफारिश की थी।<br>• <b>राजीव कुमार</b> नीति आयोग के पूर्व उपाध्यक्ष हैं, 16वें वित्त आयोग के सदस्य नहीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000075223","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Emergency & Constitutional Amendment","question":{"en":"In India, which Constitutional Amendment Act is popularly known as the “Mini-Constitution”? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में कौन-सा संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम लोकप्रिय रूप से \"लघु संविधान\" कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7<sup>th</sup> Amendment Act","hi":"7वाँ संशोधन अधिनियम"},"2":{"en":"42<sup>nd</sup> Amendment Act","hi":"42वाँ संशोधन अधिनियम"},"3":{"en":"44<sup>th</sup> Amendment Act","hi":"44वाँ संशोधन अधिनियम"},"4":{"en":"73<sup>rd</sup> Amendment Act","hi":"73वाँ संशोधन अधिनियम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 42<sup>nd</sup> Amendment Act</b><br>The <b>42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976</b>, enacted during the Emergency, is called the <b>\"Mini-Constitution\"</b> because it made the most sweeping changes to the Constitution — adding fundamental duties, amending the Preamble and transferring subjects from the state to the concurrent list.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 42nd Amendment added the words <b>\"socialist, secular and integrity\"</b> to the Preamble and inserted <b>Part IVA on Fundamental Duties</b> (Article 51A), on the recommendation of the Swaran Singh Committee.<br>• It curtailed judicial review, extended the term of the Lok Sabha to six years and shifted education, forests, weights and measures and protection of wild animals to the concurrent list.<br>• The <b>44th Amendment (1978)</b> by the Janata government reversed many of its provisions and restored the Lok Sabha term to five years.<br>• The <b>7th Amendment (1956)</b> reorganised states on linguistic lines, and the <b>73rd Amendment (1992)</b> gave constitutional status to panchayats.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 42वाँ संशोधन अधिनियम</b><br>आपातकाल के दौरान पारित <b>42वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1976</b> <b>\"लघु संविधान\"</b> कहलाता है, क्योंकि इसने संविधान में सर्वाधिक व्यापक परिवर्तन किए — मूल कर्तव्य जोड़े, प्रस्तावना संशोधित की तथा विषय राज्य सूची से समवर्ती सूची में स्थानांतरित किए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 42वें संशोधन ने प्रस्तावना में <b>\"समाजवादी, पंथनिरपेक्ष व अखंडता\"</b> शब्द जोड़े तथा स्वर्ण सिंह समिति की सिफारिश पर <b>मूल कर्तव्यों वाला भाग IVA</b> (अनुच्छेद 51A) जोड़ा।<br>• इसने न्यायिक पुनर्विलोकन में कटौती की, लोकसभा का कार्यकाल छह वर्ष किया तथा शिक्षा, वन, बाट-माप तथा वन्य जीव संरक्षण को समवर्ती सूची में डाला।<br>• जनता सरकार के <b>44वें संशोधन (1978)</b> ने इसके अनेक प्रावधान उलट दिए तथा लोकसभा का कार्यकाल पुनः पाँच वर्ष किया।<br>• <b>7वें संशोधन (1956)</b> ने भाषाई आधार पर राज्यों का पुनर्गठन किया, तथा <b>73वें संशोधन (1992)</b> ने पंचायतों को संवैधानिक दर्जा दिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000075224","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank:<br>Integration of the economy of the country with the world economy is known as ______. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रिक्त स्थान भरिए:<br>देश की अर्थव्यवस्था का विश्व अर्थव्यवस्था के साथ एकीकरण ______ कहलाता है। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Globalisation","hi":"वैश्वीकरण"},"2":{"en":"Nationalisation","hi":"राष्ट्रीयकरण"},"3":{"en":"Disinvestment","hi":"विनिवेश"},"4":{"en":"Liberalisation","hi":"उदारीकरण"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Globalisation</b><br><b>Globalisation</b> is the <b>integration of a country’s economy with the world economy</b> through trade, capital flows, technology, investment and migration. In India it began in earnest with the <b>New Economic Policy of 1991</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Globalisation involves the free movement of <b>goods, services, capital and labour</b>, and is supported by reductions in tariffs, removal of quantitative restrictions and liberal foreign investment rules.<br>• It is accompanied by <b>liberalisation</b> (removal of controls on domestic economic activity) and <b>privatisation</b> (transfer of public enterprises to private hands).<br>• India joined the <b>WTO in 1995</b> and reduced tariffs; foreign direct investment was opened up across sectors with automatic routes.<br>• Benefits include technology transfer, exports and consumer choice; critics point to job losses in unorganised sectors, inequality and vulnerability to global shocks.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – वैश्वीकरण</b><br><b>वैश्वीकरण</b> <b>किसी देश की अर्थव्यवस्था का विश्व अर्थव्यवस्था के साथ एकीकरण</b> है — व्यापार, पूँजी प्रवाह, तकनीक, निवेश व प्रवास के माध्यम से। भारत में यह <b>1991 की नई आर्थिक नीति</b> से पूर्ण रूप से आरंभ हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वैश्वीकरण में <b>वस्तुओं, सेवाओं, पूँजी व श्रम</b> की मुक्त गतिशीलता सम्मिलित है, जो दरों में कमी, मात्रात्मक प्रतिबंधों की समाप्ति तथा उदार विदेशी निवेश नियमों से समर्थित है।<br>• इसके साथ <b>उदारीकरण</b> (घरेलू आर्थिक गतिविधि पर नियंत्रण हटाना) तथा <b>निजीकरण</b> (सार्वजनिक उपक्रमों का निजी हाथों में हस्तांतरण) आते हैं।<br>• भारत <b>1995 में WTO</b> में सम्मिलित हुआ तथा दरें घटीं; विभिन्न क्षेत्रों में स्वचालित मार्ग से प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश खोला गया।<br>• लाभों में तकनीक हस्तांतरण, निर्यात व उपभोक्ता विकल्प आते हैं; आलोचक असंगठित क्षेत्र में रोजगार हानि, असमानता तथा वैश्विक आघातों के प्रति संवेदनशीलता की ओर संकेत करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000075225","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"According to the Urban and Regional Development Plans Formulation and Implementation (URDPFI) Guidelines, <b>2014</b>, which of the following concepts is associated with climate change mitigation? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शहरी एवं क्षेत्रीय विकास योजना निर्माण एवं क्रियान्वयन (URDPFI) दिशानिर्देश, <b>2014</b> के अनुसार निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी अवधारणा जलवायु परिवर्तन शमन से संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Compact Housing","hi":"सघन आवास"},"2":{"en":"Green Building","hi":"हरित भवन"},"3":{"en":"Vertical Zoning","hi":"ऊर्ध्वाधर ज़ोनिंग"},"4":{"en":"Transit Housing","hi":"पारगमन आवास"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Green Building</b><br>The URDPFI Guidelines, 2014 associate <b>green buildings</b> with <b>climate change mitigation</b> — energy-efficient design, use of renewable energy, water conservation, waste management and reduced carbon emissions from buildings, which account for a large share of urban energy use.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The URDPFI Guidelines were issued by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs in <b>2015</b> (replacing the 1996 guidelines) and provide the framework for development plans.<br>• Climate mitigation measures in urban planning include <b>green buildings, energy-efficient transport, transit-oriented development, compact city form and urban greenery</b>.<br>• Green building certification in India is given by <b>GRIHA (TERI) and IGBC (CII)</b>; the Energy Conservation Building Code sets efficiency norms.<br>• Adaptation measures, in contrast, deal with heat action plans, urban flooding and water security.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – हरित भवन</b><br>URDPFI दिशानिर्देश, 2014 <b>हरित भवनों</b> को <b>जलवायु परिवर्तन शमन</b> से जोड़ते हैं — ऊर्जा-दक्ष डिज़ाइन, नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा का उपयोग, जल संरक्षण, अपशिष्ट प्रबंधन तथा भवनों से कम कार्बन उत्सर्जन, क्योंकि भवन शहरी ऊर्जा उपयोग का बड़ा भाग लेते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• URDPFI दिशानिर्देश आवास एवं शहरी कार्य मंत्रालय ने <b>2015</b> में जारी किए (1996 के दिशानिर्देशों के स्थान पर) और ये विकास योजनाओं का ढाँचा देते हैं।<br>• शहरी योजना में जलवायु शमन उपायों में <b>हरित भवन, ऊर्जा-दक्ष परिवहन, पारगमन-उन्मुख विकास, सघन नगर रूप तथा शहरी हरित क्षेत्र</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• भारत में हरित भवन प्रमाणन <b>GRIHA (टेरी) व IGBC (CII)</b> देते हैं; ऊर्जा संरक्षण भवन संहिता दक्षता मानक निर्धारित करती है।<br>• इसके विपरीत अनुकूलन उपाय ताप कार्य योजनाओं, शहरी बाढ़ तथा जल सुरक्षा से संबंधित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000075226","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"What major policy action was taken during the \"Three Annual Plans\" of India (<b>1966–1969</b>), colloquially called the \"Plan Holiday\"? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत की \"तीन वार्षिक योजनाओं\" (<b>1966–1969</b>), जिन्हें सामान्यतः \"योजना अवकाश\" कहा जाता है, के दौरान कौन-सी प्रमुख नीतिगत कार्रवाई की गई? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nationalization of major commercial banks","hi":"प्रमुख वाणिज्यिक बैंकों का राष्ट्रीयकरण"},"2":{"en":"Implementation of new agricultural strategies","hi":"नई कृषि रणनीतियों का क्रियान्वयन"},"3":{"en":"Initiation of structural economic reforms","hi":"संरचनात्मक आर्थिक सुधारों का शुभारंभ"},"4":{"en":"Mandatory implementation of population restrictions","hi":"जनसंख्या नियंत्रण का अनिवार्य क्रियान्वयन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Implementation of new agricultural strategies</b><br>During the Plan Holiday of <b>1966–1969</b>, the Fourth Plan could not be started because of drought, a foreign exchange crisis and the war, and the government focused on <b>new agricultural strategies</b> — the High Yielding Varieties Programme and the Green Revolution package of seeds, fertilisers, irrigation and price support.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The plan holiday followed the failure of the Third Plan (1961–66), whose targets were upset by the <b>1962 and 1965 wars</b> and consecutive droughts.<br>• The new agricultural strategy was implemented from <b>1966–67</b> with the introduction of HYV wheat and rice, and the <b>Agricultural Prices Commission</b> and FCI were set up to support it.<br>• The <b>Fourth Plan (1969–74)</b> adopted the slogan \"growth with stability and progressive achievement of self-reliance\".<br>• The nationalisation of 14 major banks took place in <b>July 1969</b>, which is at the end of the plan holiday period and generally linked to the Fourth Plan era.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – नई कृषि रणनीतियों का क्रियान्वयन</b><br><b>1966–1969</b> के योजना अवकाश के दौरान सूखा, विदेशी मुद्रा संकट तथा युद्ध के कारण चौथी योजना आरंभ नहीं हो सकी और सरकार ने <b>नई कृषि रणनीतियों</b> — उच्च उपज किस्म कार्यक्रम तथा बीज, उर्वरक, सिंचाई व मूल्य समर्थन के हरित क्रांति पैकेज — पर ध्यान दिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• योजना अवकाश तीसरी योजना (1961–66) की विफलता के बाद आया, जिसके लक्ष्य <b>1962 व 1965 के युद्धों</b> तथा लगातार सूखे से बिगड़ गए।<br>• नई कृषि रणनीति <b>1966–67</b> से उच्च उपज किस्म के गेहूँ व चावल के साथ लागू हुई, और इसके समर्थन हेतु <b>कृषि मूल्य आयोग</b> तथा FCI की स्थापना हुई।<br>• <b>चौथी योजना (1969–74)</b> ने \"स्थिरता के साथ विकास तथा आत्मनिर्भरता की क्रमिक प्राप्ति\" का नारा अपनाया।<br>• 14 प्रमुख बैंकों का राष्ट्रीयकरण <b>जुलाई 1969</b> में हुआ, जो योजना अवकाश के अंत में है और सामान्यतः चौथी योजना काल से जोड़ा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000075227","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"During a transit, a planet blocks <b>1%</b> of its star's light. Assuming the star has uniform brightness, what is the ratio of the planet's radius to the star's radius? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक पारगमन के दौरान ग्रह अपने तारे के प्रकाश का <b>1%</b> अवरुद्ध करता है। यह मानते हुए कि तारे की चमक एकसमान है, ग्रह की त्रिज्या तथा तारे की त्रिज्या का अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.01"},"2":{"en":"0.1"},"3":{"en":"0.2"},"4":{"en":"0.5"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 0.1</b><br>The drop in brightness during a transit equals the ratio of the areas: \\(\\frac{\\Delta F}{F} = \\left(\\frac{R_p}{R_s}\\right)^2 = 0.01\\). Hence \\(\\frac{R_p}{R_s} = \\sqrt{0.01} = 0.1\\), so the planet’s radius is one-tenth of the star’s radius.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The transit method detects exoplanets by the periodic dimming of a star as a planet passes in front of it; the depth of the dip gives the <b>size ratio</b> of the planet and star.<br>• A planet of Jupiter’s size crossing a Sun-like star produces a dip of about <b>1%</b>, while an Earth-sized planet gives a dip of about 0.008%.<br>• The transit method was used by the <b>Kepler</b> mission and is planned for the <b>PLATO</b> mission; India’s proposed ExoWorlds mission will also use it.<br>• Transit geometry requires the planet’s orbit to be nearly edge-on to the observer, and repeated transits give the orbital period.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 0.1</b><br>पारगमन के समय चमक में गिरावट क्षेत्रफलों के अनुपात के बराबर होती है: \\(\\frac{\\Delta F}{F} = \\left(\\frac{R_p}{R_s}\\right)^2 = 0.01\\)। अतः \\(\\frac{R_p}{R_s} = \\sqrt{0.01} = 0.1\\), अर्थात् ग्रह की त्रिज्या तारे की त्रिज्या की एक-दसवीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पारगमन विधि बहिर्ग्रहों का पता तारे की आवधिक मंदता से लगाती है, जब ग्रह उसके सामने से गुजरता है; गिरावट की गहराई ग्रह व तारे के <b>आकार अनुपात</b> देती है।<br>• सूर्य जैसे तारे के सामने बृहस्पति आकार का ग्रह लगभग <b>1%</b> तथा पृथ्वी आकार का ग्रह लगभग 0.008% मंदता उत्पन्न करता है।<br>• पारगमन विधि <b>केप्लर</b> मिशन में प्रयुक्त हुई तथा <b>PLATO</b> मिशन हेतु प्रस्तावित है; भारत का प्रस्तावित एक्सोवर्ल्ड्स मिशन भी इसका उपयोग करेगा।<br>• पारगमन हेतु ग्रह की कक्षा पर्यवेक्षक की दृष्टि के लगभग समांतर होनी चाहिए, तथा बार-बार पारगमन से कक्षीय आवर्तकाल मिलता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000075228","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Who among the following is primarily credited with introducing the Ryotwari system in the Madras Presidency? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किसे मुख्यतः मद्रास प्रेसीडेंसी में रैयतवाड़ी व्यवस्था लागू करने का श्रेय दिया जाता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Holt Mackenzie","hi":"होल्ट मैकेंज़ी"},"2":{"en":"Thomas Munro","hi":"थॉमस मुनरो"},"3":{"en":"Cornwallis","hi":"कॉर्नवॉलिस"},"4":{"en":"William Bentinck","hi":"विलियम बेंटिक"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Thomas Munro</b><br><b>Thomas Munro</b>, Governor of Madras (1820–27), is primarily credited with introducing and extending the <b>Ryotwari system</b> in the Madras Presidency, in which land revenue was settled directly with the individual cultivator (ryot) for a period of years.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Ryotwari system was first tried by <b>Alexander Read</b> in Baramahal and Salem and developed by Munro; it was later extended to Bombay by Elphinstone.<br>• Under Ryotwari, the <b>ryot held the land as long as he paid the revenue</b>, which was based on an estimate of the soil and produce and revised periodically.<br>• The <b>Permanent Settlement (1793)</b> of Cornwallis created zamindars in Bengal, while the <b>Mahalwari system</b> (Holt Mackenzie, 1822) settled revenue with village communities in the North-Western Provinces.<br>• These revenue systems shaped agrarian relations, led to peasant indebtedness and were an important cause of rural unrest in the nineteenth century.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – थॉमस मुनरो</b><br>मद्रास के गवर्नर (1820–27) <b>थॉमस मुनरो</b> को मुख्यतः मद्रास प्रेसीडेंसी में <b>रैयतवाड़ी व्यवस्था</b> लागू करने व विस्तारित करने का श्रेय दिया जाता है, जिसमें भू-राजस्व वर्षों की अवधि हेतु सीधे व्यक्तिगत कृषक (रैयत) से तय किया जाता था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• रैयतवाड़ी व्यवस्था पहले <b>अलेक्जेंडर रीड</b> ने बारामहल व सेलम में प्रयोग की और मुनरो ने विकसित की; बाद में एल्फिंस्टन ने इसे बंबई तक बढ़ाया।<br>• रैयतवाड़ी में <b>रैयत भूमि तब तक रखता था जब तक राजस्व देता रहे</b>, जो मृदा व उपज के अनुमान पर आधारित होकर समय-समय पर संशोधित होता था।<br>• कॉर्नवॉलिस का <b>स्थायी बंदोबस्त (1793)</b> बंगाल में जमींदार बनाया, जबकि <b>महालवाड़ी व्यवस्था</b> (होल्ट मैकेंज़ी, 1822) ने उत्तर-पश्चिमी प्रांतों में ग्राम समुदायों से राजस्व तय किया।<br>• इन राजस्व व्यवस्थाओं ने कृषि संबंधों को आकार दिया, किसानों का ऋण बढ़ाया तथा उन्नीसवीं शताब्दी में ग्रामीण अशांति का महत्वपूर्ण कारण बनीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000075229","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"A region experiences rapid deforestation followed by irregular river flow, floods during monsoon, and drought afterward. Which ecological principle does this most strongly demonstrate? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी क्षेत्र में तीव्र वनोन्मूलन के बाद नदी प्रवाह में अनियमितता, मानसून में बाढ़ तथा उसके बाद सूखा देखा जाता है। यह किस पारिस्थितिक सिद्धांत को सर्वाधिक बलपूर्वक प्रदर्शित करता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Competitive exclusion among species for water resources","hi":"जल संसाधनों हेतु प्रजातियों के बीच प्रतिस्पर्धी बहिष्करण"},"2":{"en":"Ecological succession after water related disturbance","hi":"जल संबंधी विक्षोभ के बाद पारिस्थितिक अनुक्रमण"},"3":{"en":"Regulation of water flow within watersheds","hi":"जलग्रहण क्षेत्रों के भीतर जल प्रवाह का नियमन"},"4":{"en":"Stabilisation of energy pyramids in water based ecosystems","hi":"जल आधारित पारितंत्रों में ऊर्जा पिरामिडों का स्थिरीकरण"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Regulation of water flow within watersheds</b><br>The sequence of deforestation, followed by irregular river flow, monsoon floods and later drought, demonstrates that <b>forests regulate water flow within a watershed</b> — their roots and leaf litter improve infiltration, reduce surface runoff and recharge groundwater, so their loss produces flash floods and dry spells.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• This is a <b>watershed function</b> of forests: interception of rainfall, reduction of soil erosion, groundwater recharge and maintenance of base flow in streams.<br>• Deforestation increases <b>surface runoff and soil erosion</b>, silts up rivers and reduces infiltration, leading to the \"flood-drought\" cycle.<br>• Watershed management programmes in India include the <b>Neeru-Meeru, Arvary Pani Sansad and the integrated watershed management programme</b> of the Department of Land Resources.<br>• The other options describe interspecific competition, succession and trophic structure, which are different ecological concepts.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जलग्रहण क्षेत्रों के भीतर जल प्रवाह का नियमन</b><br>वनोन्मूलन के बाद नदी प्रवाह में अनियमितता, मानसून में बाढ़ तथा बाद में सूखे का क्रम दर्शाता है कि <b>वन जलग्रहण क्षेत्र में जल प्रवाह का नियमन</b> करते हैं — जड़ें व पत्ती-पर्ण कुंड अंतःस्रवण बढ़ाते, पृष्ठ अपवाह घटाते तथा भूजल पुनर्भरण करते हैं, अतः उनके ह्रास से अचानक बाढ़ व सूखा आता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह वनों का <b>जलग्रहण कार्य</b> है — वर्षा का अवरोधन, मृदा अपरदन में कमी, भूजल पुनर्भरण तथा धाराओं में आधार प्रवाह बनाए रखना।<br>• वनोन्मूलन से <b>पृष्ठ अपवाह व मृदा अपरदन</b> बढ़ता है, नदियाँ गादयुक्त होती हैं और अंतःस्रवण घटने से \"बाढ़-सूखा\" चक्र बनता है।<br>• भारत में जलग्रहण प्रबंधन कार्यक्रमों में <b>नीरू-मीरू, अर्वरी पानी संसद तथा भूमि संसाधन विभाग का समेकित जलग्रहण प्रबंधन कार्यक्रम</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• शेष विकल्प अंतरा-विशिष्ट प्रतिस्पर्धा, अनुक्रमण तथा पोषण-स्तरीय संरचना के भिन्न पारिस्थितिक सिद्धांतों का वर्णन करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000075230","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Microeconomics","question":{"en":"A university raises its tuition fee by <b>20%</b>. As a result, student enrolment decreases by <b>30%</b>, while all other factors remain unchanged. Which of the following statements correctly describes the price elasticity of demand and the resulting change in the university's total tuition revenue? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी विश्वविद्यालय ने अपना ट्यूशन शुल्क <b>20%</b> बढ़ाया। परिणामस्वरूप विद्यार्थियों का नामांकन <b>30%</b> घट गया, जबकि अन्य सभी कारक अपरिवर्तित रहे। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन माँग की कीमत लोच तथा विश्वविद्यालय के कुल ट्यूशन राजस्व में परिवर्तन का सही वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Demand is inelastic, and total tuition revenue increases.","hi":"माँग बेलोचदार है तथा कुल ट्यूशन राजस्व बढ़ता है।"},"2":{"en":"Demand is elastic, and total tuition revenue decreases.","hi":"माँग लोचदार है तथा कुल ट्यूशन राजस्व घटता है।"},"3":{"en":"Demand is unit elastic, and total tuition revenue remains unchanged.","hi":"माँग इकाई लोचदार है तथा कुल ट्यूशन राजस्व अपरिवर्तित रहता है।"},"4":{"en":"Demand is perfectly elastic, and total tuition revenue becomes zero.","hi":"माँग पूर्णतः लोचदार है तथा कुल ट्यूशन राजस्व शून्य हो जाता है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Demand is elastic, and total tuition revenue decreases.</b><br>The price elasticity of demand = percentage change in quantity ÷ percentage change in price = 30 ÷ 20 = <b>1.5</b>, which is greater than one, so demand is <b>elastic</b>. When demand is elastic, a price rise reduces total revenue, because the fall in enrolment (30%) outweighs the rise in fees (20%), so <b>total tuition revenue falls</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• If elasticity is greater than 1, demand is elastic; equal to 1, unit elastic; and less than 1, inelastic.<br>• Total revenue increases with a price rise only when demand is <b>inelastic</b>; it falls when demand is elastic, and is maximum at unit elasticity.<br>• Determinants of elasticity include the availability of <b>substitutes, share of income spent, necessity nature and time period</b>; education at a particular university has many substitutes, so it is elastic.<br>• Elasticity is measured by the formula \\(E_d = \\frac{\\%\\ \\text{change in quantity demanded}}{\\%\\ \\text{change in price}}\\), and its numerical value is taken as positive.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – माँग लोचदार है तथा कुल ट्यूशन राजस्व घटता है।</b><br>माँग की कीमत लोच = मात्रा में प्रतिशत परिवर्तन ÷ कीमत में प्रतिशत परिवर्तन = 30 ÷ 20 = <b>1.5</b>, जो एक से अधिक है, अतः माँग <b>लोचदार</b> है। जब माँग लोचदार होती है तो कीमत वृद्धि से कुल राजस्व घटता है, क्योंकि नामांकन में 30% की गिरावट शुल्क में 20% वृद्धि से अधिक है, अतः <b>कुल ट्यूशन राजस्व घटता है</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यदि लोच 1 से अधिक हो तो माँग लोचदार, 1 के बराबर हो तो इकाई लोचदार तथा 1 से कम हो तो बेलोचदार होती है।<br>• कीमत बढ़ने पर कुल राजस्व तभी बढ़ता है जब माँग <b>बेलोचदार</b> हो; लोचदार माँग में वह घटता है, तथा इकाई लोच पर अधिकतम होता है।<br>• लोच के निर्धारक हैं — <b>स्थानापन्न वस्तुओं की उपलब्धता, आय का भाग, आवश्यकता की प्रकृति तथा समय</b>; किसी विशेष विश्वविद्यालय की शिक्षा के अनेक स्थानापन्न हैं, अतः वह लोचदार है।<br>• लोच का सूत्र माँगी गई मात्रा में प्रतिशत परिवर्तन को कीमत में प्रतिशत परिवर्तन से विभाजित करके है तथा इसका संख्यात्मक मान धनात्मक लिया जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000075231","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"One third of a certain journey is covered at a speed of 24 km/hr, one fourth at a speed of 36 km/hr and the remaining at a speed of 60 km/hr. What will be the average speed for the entire journey? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी यात्रा का एक-तिहाई भाग 24 km/hr की चाल से, एक-चौथाई भाग 36 km/hr की चाल से और शेष भाग 60 km/hr की चाल से तय किया जाता है। पूरी यात्रा की औसत चाल क्या होगी? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"22 km/h"},"2":{"en":"30 km/h"},"3":{"en":"28 km/h"},"4":{"en":"36 km/h"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let distance = 12 km → parts = 4, 3, 5 km<br>Time = \\(\\frac{4}{24} + \\frac{3}{36} + \\frac{5}{60} = \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{12} + \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{1}{3}\\) hr<br>Average speed = \\(\\frac{12}{1/3} = \\boxed{36}\\) km/h<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 36 km/h.</b>","hi":"माना दूरी = 12 km → भाग = 4, 3, 5 km<br>समय = \\(\\frac{4}{24} + \\frac{3}{36} + \\frac{5}{60} = \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{12} + \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{1}{3}\\) घंटा<br>औसत चाल = \\(\\frac{12}{1/3} = \\boxed{36}\\) km/h<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 36 km/h है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000075232","section":"MATH","topic":"Pipe and Cistern","question":{"en":"A tank, which can normally be filled in 15 hours, takes 5 additional hours to fill due to a leak at the bottom. If the tank is completely full, how long will the leak alone take to empty it? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक टंकी, जो सामान्यतः 15 घंटे में भर जाती है, तली में रिसाव के कारण भरने में 5 घंटे अधिक लेती है। यदि टंकी पूरी भरी हो, तो अकेला रिसाव उसे कितने समय में खाली करेगा? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30 hours","hi":"30 घंटे"},"2":{"en":"40 hours","hi":"40 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"50 hours","hi":"50 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"60 hours","hi":"60 घंटे"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Tank = LCM(15, 20) = 60 units<br>Pipe = 4/hr, Pipe − Leak = 3/hr → Leak = 1/hr<br>Leak alone = \\(\\frac{60}{1} = \\boxed{60}\\) hours<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 60 hours.</b>","hi":"टंकी = LCM(15, 20) = 60 इकाई<br>पाइप = 4/घंटा, पाइप − रिसाव = 3/घंटा → रिसाव = 1/घंटा<br>अकेला रिसाव = \\(\\frac{60}{1} = \\boxed{60}\\) घंटे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 60 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000075233","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"Two persons, A and B, begin traveling simultaneously from points X and Y toward each other. The speed of A is 20% greater than the speed of B. After they meet at a point on the way, A takes 2.5 hours to reach Y and B takes a hours to reach X. Find the value of a. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो व्यक्ति, A और B, बिंदुओं X और Y से एक साथ एक-दूसरे की ओर चलना शुरू करते हैं। A की चाल B की चाल से 20% अधिक है। रास्ते में एक बिंदु पर मिलने के बाद, A को Y तक पहुँचने में 2.5 घंटे और B को X तक पहुँचने में a घंटे लगते हैं। a का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2.8 hours","hi":"2.8 घंटे"},"2":{"en":"3 hours","hi":"3 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"3.6 hours","hi":"3.6 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"4 hours","hi":"4 घंटे"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{S_A}{S_B} = \\sqrt{\\frac{t_B}{t_A}}\\) (times after meeting)<br>\\(\\frac{6}{5} = \\sqrt{\\frac{a}{2.5}} \\Rightarrow \\frac{a}{2.5} = \\frac{36}{25}\\)<br>\\(a = \\boxed{3.6}\\) hours<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3.6 hours.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{S_A}{S_B} = \\sqrt{\\frac{t_B}{t_A}}\\) (मिलने के बाद के समय)<br>\\(\\frac{6}{5} = \\sqrt{\\frac{a}{2.5}} \\Rightarrow \\frac{a}{2.5} = \\frac{36}{25}\\)<br>\\(a = \\boxed{3.6}\\) घंटे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3.6 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000075234","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"Find the area of the rectangle formed by the graphs of x = 0, x = 4, y = 0, and y = 3. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"x = 0, x = 4, y = 0 और y = 3 के आलेखों से बने आयत का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7 square units","hi":"7 वर्ग इकाई"},"2":{"en":"12 square units","hi":"12 वर्ग इकाई"},"3":{"en":"14 square units","hi":"14 वर्ग इकाई"},"4":{"en":"10 square units","hi":"10 वर्ग इकाई"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"200\" height=\"142\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 142\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M10 120H190M30 135V10\"/><path d=\"M184 116l6 4-6 4M26 16l4-6 4 6\"/><path d=\"M30 30H150V120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"26\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x = 4</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\">y = 3</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"134\">x</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"16\">y</text></g></svg><br>Length = 4 − 0 = 4, Breadth = 3 − 0 = 3<br>Area = \\(4 \\times 3 = \\boxed{12}\\) square units<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 12 square units.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"200\" height=\"142\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 142\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M10 120H190M30 135V10\"/><path d=\"M184 116l6 4-6 4M26 16l4-6 4 6\"/><path d=\"M30 30H150V120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"26\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x = 4</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\">y = 3</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"134\">x</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"16\">y</text></g></svg><br>लंबाई = 4 − 0 = 4, चौड़ाई = 3 − 0 = 3<br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(4 \\times 3 = \\boxed{12}\\) वर्ग इकाई<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 12 वर्ग इकाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000075235","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"The lines x - y = 0, x + y = 0, and y = k form a triangle. If the area of this triangle is 25 sq. units, what is the value of k? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रेखाएँ x - y = 0, x + y = 0 और y = k एक त्रिभुज बनाती हैं। यदि इस त्रिभुज का क्षेत्रफल 25 वर्ग इकाई है, तो k का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"k = 5 or −5","hi":"k = 5 या −5"},"2":{"en":"k = -10 or 10","hi":"k = -10 या 10"},"3":{"en":"k = 25 or -25","hi":"k = 25 या -25"},"4":{"en":"k = -20 or 20","hi":"k = -20 या 20"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 120H220M120 140V10\"/><path d=\"M45 45L120 120L195 45\"/><path d=\"M40 60H200\"/><path d=\"M60 60L120 120L180 60Z\" fill=\"#ddd\" fill-opacity=\"0.6\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"116\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"192\" y=\"40\">y = x</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"end\">y = −x</text><text x=\"204\" y=\"64\">y = k</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"76\">(k, k)</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\">(−k, k)</text></g></svg><br>Vertices: (0, 0), (k, k), (−k, k)<br>Area = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 2|k| \\times |k| = k^2\\)<br>\\(k^2 = 25 \\Rightarrow k = \\boxed{\\pm 5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): k = 5 or −5.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 120H220M120 140V10\"/><path d=\"M45 45L120 120L195 45\"/><path d=\"M40 60H200\"/><path d=\"M60 60L120 120L180 60Z\" fill=\"#ddd\" fill-opacity=\"0.6\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"116\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"192\" y=\"40\">y = x</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"end\">y = −x</text><text x=\"204\" y=\"64\">y = k</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"76\">(k, k)</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\">(−k, k)</text></g></svg><br>शीर्ष: (0, 0), (k, k), (−k, k)<br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 2|k| \\times |k| = k^2\\)<br>\\(k^2 = 25 \\Rightarrow k = \\boxed{\\pm 5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): k = 5 या −5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000075236","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A solid metallic cube with a surface area of 96 cm² is melted to form smaller cubes with a surface area of 24 cm² each. Find the number of smaller cubes. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"96 cm² पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल वाले धातु के एक ठोस घन को पिघलाकर 24 cm² पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल वाले छोटे घन बनाए जाते हैं। छोटे घनों की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"14"},"2":{"en":"6"},"3":{"en":"18"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">a</text></g></svg><br>Big cube: \\(6a^2 = 96 \\Rightarrow a = 4\\) cm; small cube: \\(6b^2 = 24 \\Rightarrow b = 2\\) cm<br>Number = \\(\\left(\\frac{4}{2}\\right)^3 = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">a</text></g></svg><br>बड़ा घन: \\(6a^2 = 96 \\Rightarrow a = 4\\) cm; छोटा घन: \\(6b^2 = 24 \\Rightarrow b = 2\\) cm<br>संख्या = \\(\\left(\\frac{4}{2}\\right)^3 = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000075237","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord of a circle subtends equal angles of 35° at two points on the same segment of the circle. What is the angle subtended by the same chord at the centre of the circle? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वृत्त की जीवा वृत्त के एक ही खंड में स्थित दो बिंदुओं पर 35° के बराबर कोण बनाती है। वही जीवा वृत्त के केंद्र पर कितना कोण बनाती है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"125°"},"2":{"en":"70°"},"3":{"en":"35°"},"4":{"en":"115°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"165\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 165 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M48 120L80 20L112 120ZM48 120L80 75L112 120\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"74\" y=\"73\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"44\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"132\">B</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\">35°</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"middle\">?</text></g></svg><br>Angle at the centre = 2 × angle at the circumference (same segment)<br>\\(\\angle AOB = 2 \\times 35^\\circ = \\boxed{70^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 70°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"165\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 165 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M48 120L80 20L112 120ZM48 120L80 75L112 120\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"74\" y=\"73\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"44\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"132\">B</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\">35°</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"middle\">?</text></g></svg><br>केंद्र पर कोण = 2 × परिधि पर कोण (उसी खंड में)<br>\\(\\angle AOB = 2 \\times 35^\\circ = \\boxed{70^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 70° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000075238","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A tower is 120 m high. The angles of depression of two points on the same straight line and on the same side of the tower are 30° and 60°. Find the distance between the two points. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक मीनार 120 m ऊँची है। मीनार के एक ही ओर एक ही सीधी रेखा पर स्थित दो बिंदुओं के अवनमन कोण 30° और 60° हैं। दोनों बिंदुओं के बीच की दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(80\\sqrt{3}\\) m"},"2":{"en":"\\(70\\sqrt{3}\\) m"},"3":{"en":"\\(100\\sqrt{3}\\) m"},"4":{"en":"\\(120\\sqrt{3}\\) m"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"262\" height=\"159\" viewBox=\"0 0 262 159\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M50 20V124H230ZM50 20L110 124\"/><path d=\"M50 116h8v8\"/><path d=\"M94 124A16 16 0 0 1 102 110\"/><path d=\"M214 124A16 16 0 0 1 216 116\"/><path d=\"M110 143H230\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"45\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"end\">B</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\">120 m</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"118\">60°</text><text x=\"233\" y=\"118\">30°</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"153\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x</text></g></svg><br>BC = \\(120\\sqrt{3}\\), BD = \\(\\frac{120}{\\sqrt{3}} = 40\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>x = CD = \\(120\\sqrt{3} - 40\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{80\\sqrt{3}}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(80\\sqrt{3}\\) m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"262\" height=\"159\" viewBox=\"0 0 262 159\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M50 20V124H230ZM50 20L110 124\"/><path d=\"M50 116h8v8\"/><path d=\"M94 124A16 16 0 0 1 102 110\"/><path d=\"M214 124A16 16 0 0 1 216 116\"/><path d=\"M110 143H230\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"45\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"end\">B</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\">120 m</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"118\">60°</text><text x=\"233\" y=\"118\">30°</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"153\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x</text></g></svg><br>BC = \\(120\\sqrt{3}\\), BD = \\(\\frac{120}{\\sqrt{3}} = 40\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>x = CD = \\(120\\sqrt{3} - 40\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{80\\sqrt{3}}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(80\\sqrt{3}\\) m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000075239","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"An isosceles trapezium has parallel sides of lengths 18 cm and 30 cm. If the length of each non-parallel side is 10 cm, find the area of the trapezium. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक समद्विबाहु समलंब चतुर्भुज की समांतर भुजाओं की लंबाई 18 cm और 30 cm है। यदि प्रत्येक असमांतर भुजा की लंबाई 10 cm है, तो समलंब चतुर्भुज का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"192 cm²"},"2":{"en":"240 cm²"},"3":{"en":"144 cm²"},"4":{"en":"288 cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"195\" height=\"79\" viewBox=\"0 0 195 79\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M50 15H140L170 55H20Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 15V55\"/><path d=\"M50 48h7v7\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"95\" y=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"39\">h</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"35\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"35\">10</text></g></svg><br>Offset on each side = \\(\\frac{30 - 18}{2} = 6\\) cm<br>\\(h = \\sqrt{10^2 - 6^2} = 8\\) cm<br>Area = \\(\\frac{1}{2}(18 + 30) \\times 8 = \\boxed{192}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 192 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"195\" height=\"79\" viewBox=\"0 0 195 79\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M50 15H140L170 55H20Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 15V55\"/><path d=\"M50 48h7v7\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"95\" y=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"39\">h</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"35\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"35\">10</text></g></svg><br>प्रत्येक ओर का अंतर = \\(\\frac{30 - 18}{2} = 6\\) cm<br>\\(h = \\sqrt{10^2 - 6^2} = 8\\) cm<br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{2}(18 + 30) \\times 8 = \\boxed{192}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 192 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000075240","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\tan\\alpha\\) and \\(\\tan\\beta\\) are roots of \\(x^2 - px + q = 0\\), find \\(\\cos^2(\\alpha + \\beta)\\). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\tan\\alpha\\) और \\(\\tan\\beta\\), \\(x^2 - px + q = 0\\) के मूल हैं, तो \\(\\cos^2(\\alpha + \\beta)\\) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1 + q^2}{p^2 + (1 + q)^2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{(1 + q)^2}{p^2 + (1 - q)^2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1 - q^2}{p^2 + (1 + q)^2}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{(1 - q)^2}{p^2 + (1 - q)^2}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan\\alpha + \\tan\\beta = p,\\ \\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta = q\\) → \\(\\tan(\\alpha + \\beta) = \\frac{p}{1 - q}\\)<br>\\(\\cos^2(\\alpha + \\beta) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\tan^2(\\alpha + \\beta)} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{p^2}{(1 - q)^2}}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{(1 - q)^2}{p^2 + (1 - q)^2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{(1 - q)^2}{p^2 + (1 - q)^2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan\\alpha + \\tan\\beta = p,\\ \\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta = q\\) → \\(\\tan(\\alpha + \\beta) = \\frac{p}{1 - q}\\)<br>\\(\\cos^2(\\alpha + \\beta) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\tan^2(\\alpha + \\beta)} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{p^2}{(1 - q)^2}}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{(1 - q)^2}{p^2 + (1 - q)^2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{(1 - q)^2}{p^2 + (1 - q)^2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000075241","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The base of a right prism is an isosceles triangle whose equal sides are 10 cm each, and the unequal base side is 12 cm. If the ratio of the numerical value of its total surface area to its volume is 2 : 1, find the altitude of the prism (in cm). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज्म का आधार एक समद्विबाहु त्रिभुज है जिसकी बराबर भुजाएँ 10 cm प्रत्येक हैं, और असमान आधार भुजा 12 cm है। यदि इसके संपूर्ण पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल और आयतन के संख्यात्मक मानों का अनुपात 2 : 1 है, तो प्रिज्म की ऊँचाई (cm में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.5 cm"},"2":{"en":"1 cm"},"3":{"en":"1.5 cm"},"4":{"en":"2 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"178\" height=\"116\" viewBox=\"0 0 178 116\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M84 18L30 90H138Z\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"94\">B</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"94\">C</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"106\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"117\" y=\"54\">10</text><text x=\"51\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text></g></svg><br>Triangle height = \\(\\sqrt{10^2 - 6^2} = 8\\) → base area = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 \\times 8 = 48\\), perimeter = 32<br>TSA = \\(2 \\times 48 + 32h\\), Volume = \\(48h\\)<br>\\(96 + 32h = 2 \\times 48h \\Rightarrow 64h = 96\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{1.5}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1.5 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"178\" height=\"116\" viewBox=\"0 0 178 116\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M84 18L30 90H138Z\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"94\">B</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"94\">C</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"106\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"117\" y=\"54\">10</text><text x=\"51\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text></g></svg><br>त्रिभुज की ऊँचाई = \\(\\sqrt{10^2 - 6^2} = 8\\) → आधार का क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 \\times 8 = 48\\), परिमाप = 32<br>संपूर्ण पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = \\(2 \\times 48 + 32h\\), आयतन = \\(48h\\)<br>\\(96 + 32h = 2 \\times 48h \\Rightarrow 64h = 96\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{1.5}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1.5 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000075242","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = \\sqrt{13}\\), then find the value of \\(\\frac{3x}{x^2 - 1}\\). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = \\sqrt{13}\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{3x}{x^2 - 1}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"±1"},"2":{"en":"±2"},"3":{"en":"±3"},"4":{"en":"±4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 = 13 - 4 = 9 \\Rightarrow x - \\frac{1}{x} = \\pm 3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3x}{x^2 - 1} = \\frac{3}{x - \\frac{1}{x}} = \\frac{3}{\\pm 3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\pm 1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ±1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 = 13 - 4 = 9 \\Rightarrow x - \\frac{1}{x} = \\pm 3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3x}{x^2 - 1} = \\frac{3}{x - \\frac{1}{x}} = \\frac{3}{\\pm 3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\pm 1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ±1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000075243","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Study the given histogram carefully, which shows the battery life of cycles (in hours) on the x-axis and the number of cycles (frequency) on the y-axis, and answer the question that follows:<br>What percentage of cycles have battery life less than 7 hours?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q63.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए आयतचित्र का ध्यानपूर्वक अध्ययन कीजिए, जो x-अक्ष पर साइकिलों की बैटरी लाइफ (घंटों में) और y-अक्ष पर साइकिलों की संख्या (आवृत्ति) दर्शाता है, और नीचे दिए गए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br>कितने प्रतिशत साइकिलों की बैटरी लाइफ 7 घंटे से कम है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q63.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"64%"},"2":{"en":"62%"},"3":{"en":"32%"},"4":{"en":"26%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Frequencies: 3, 10, 18, 16, 3 → Total = 50<br>Less than 7 hours = 3 + 10 = 13<br>\\(\\frac{13}{50} \\times 100 = \\boxed{26\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 26%.</b>","hi":"आवृत्तियाँ: 3, 10, 18, 16, 3 → कुल = 50<br>7 घंटे से कम = 3 + 10 = 13<br>\\(\\frac{13}{50} \\times 100 = \\boxed{26\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 26% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q63.jpg"]}},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000075244","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A vessel has 45 liters of a solution of alcohol and water, having 60% alcohol. How many liters of the solution must be withdrawn from the vessel and replaced by the same quantity of water so that the resulting solution would have 35% alcohol? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक बर्तन में 45 लीटर अल्कोहल और पानी का विलयन है, जिसमें 60% अल्कोहल है। बर्तन से कितने लीटर विलयन निकालकर उतनी ही मात्रा में पानी मिलाया जाए कि परिणामी विलयन में 35% अल्कोहल हो? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15.25 liters","hi":"15.25 लीटर"},"2":{"en":"18.75 liters","hi":"18.75 लीटर"},"3":{"en":"20.50 liters","hi":"20.50 लीटर"},"4":{"en":"23.85 liters","hi":"23.85 लीटर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(60\\% \\times \\left(1 - \\frac{x}{45}\\right) = 35\\%\\)<br>\\(1 - \\frac{x}{45} = \\frac{7}{12} \\Rightarrow \\frac{x}{45} = \\frac{5}{12}\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{18.75}\\) L<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 18.75 liters.</b>","hi":"\\(60\\% \\times \\left(1 - \\frac{x}{45}\\right) = 35\\%\\)<br>\\(1 - \\frac{x}{45} = \\frac{7}{12} \\Rightarrow \\frac{x}{45} = \\frac{5}{12}\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{18.75}\\) L<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 18.75 लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000075245","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"Two right circular cylinders have equal volumes. If the ratio of their heights is 9: 16, find the ratio of their radii. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो लंब वृत्तीय बेलनों के आयतन बराबर हैं। यदि उनकी ऊँचाइयों का अनुपात 9: 16 है, तो उनकी त्रिज्याओं का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3:4"},"2":{"en":"2:3"},"3":{"en":"4:3"},"4":{"en":"3:2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">r₁</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">9k</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">r₂</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">16k</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\pi r_1^2 \\times 9k = \\pi r_2^2 \\times 16k\\)<br>\\(\\frac{r_1^2}{r_2^2} = \\frac{16}{9}\\)<br>\\(r_1 : r_2 = \\boxed{4 : 3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 4:3.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">r₁</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">9k</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">r₂</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">16k</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\pi r_1^2 \\times 9k = \\pi r_2^2 \\times 16k\\)<br>\\(\\frac{r_1^2}{r_2^2} = \\frac{16}{9}\\)<br>\\(r_1 : r_2 = \\boxed{4 : 3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 4:3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000075246","section":"MATH","topic":"Discount","question":{"en":"A product is marked at ₹25,000. It is sold at a discount of 10% and then at a further discount such that its final selling price becomes ₹20,250. What is the percentage of the second discount? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक उत्पाद पर ₹25,000 अंकित है। इसे 10% छूट पर और फिर एक और छूट पर बेचा जाता है जिससे इसका अंतिम विक्रय मूल्य ₹20,250 हो जाता है। दूसरी छूट का प्रतिशत क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12.25%"},"2":{"en":"10%"},"3":{"en":"14.40%"},"4":{"en":"16%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"After 10% discount = \\(25000 \\times 0.9 = 22500\\)<br>Second discount = 22500 − 20250 = 2250<br>% = \\(\\frac{2250}{22500} \\times 100 = \\boxed{10\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 10%.</b>","hi":"10% छूट के बाद = \\(25000 \\times 0.9 = 22500\\)<br>दूसरी छूट = 22500 − 20250 = 2250<br>% = \\(\\frac{2250}{22500} \\times 100 = \\boxed{10\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 10% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000075247","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The following pie-chart presents the percentage distribution of the population across five different regions. Study the pie-chart carefully and answer the question based on the provided data.<br>If the population of Region A is 70,000, what is the population of Region E?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q67.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित पाई-चार्ट पाँच विभिन्न क्षेत्रों में जनसंख्या का प्रतिशत वितरण प्रस्तुत करता है। पाई-चार्ट का ध्यानपूर्वक अध्ययन कीजिए और दिए गए आँकड़ों के आधार पर प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br>यदि क्षेत्र A की जनसंख्या 70,000 है, तो क्षेत्र E की जनसंख्या क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q67.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25,000"},"2":{"en":"30,000"},"3":{"en":"35,000"},"4":{"en":"40,000"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From the chart: Region A = 28%, Region E = 12%<br>28% = 70000 → 1% = 2500<br>Region E = \\(12 \\times 2500 = \\boxed{30000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 30,000.</b>","hi":"चार्ट से: क्षेत्र A = 28%, क्षेत्र E = 12%<br>28% = 70000 → 1% = 2500<br>क्षेत्र E = \\(12 \\times 2500 = \\boxed{30000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 30,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q67.jpg"]}},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000075248","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Read the following frequency polygon which represents class interval (Time Spent in Mall (Minutes)) on the x-axis and frequency (Number of Visitors) on the y-axis, and answer the following question:<br>Using the standard continuous distribution formula for estimating statistical parameters, what is the approximate Median time (in minutes) spent by a visitor on Weekdays?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q68.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित आवृत्ति बहुभुज को पढ़िए, जो x-अक्ष पर वर्ग अंतराल (मॉल में बिताया गया समय (मिनट)) और y-अक्ष पर आवृत्ति (आगंतुकों की संख्या) दर्शाता है, और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br>सांख्यिकीय प्राचलों के आकलन के लिए मानक सतत बंटन सूत्र का उपयोग करते हुए, सप्ताह के कार्यदिवसों में एक आगंतुक द्वारा बिताया गया लगभग माध्यिका समय (मिनटों में) क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q68.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"65.5 minutes","hi":"65.5 मिनट"},"2":{"en":"90.5 minutes","hi":"90.5 मिनट"},"3":{"en":"71.5 minutes","hi":"71.5 मिनट"},"4":{"en":"83.5 minutes","hi":"83.5 मिनट"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Class</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">0-30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30-60</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">60-90</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">90-120</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">120-150</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">150-180</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">180-210</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">f</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">0</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">34</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">100</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">85</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">0</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">cf</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">0</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">34</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">134</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">219</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">249</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">271</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">271</td></tr></table>N = 271 → \\(\\frac{N}{2} = 135.5\\) → median class 90–120 (l = 90, cf = 134, f = 85, h = 30)<br>Median = \\(90 + \\frac{135.5 - 134}{85} \\times 30 = 90 + 0.53 \\approx \\boxed{90.5}\\) min<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 90.5 minutes.</b>","hi":"<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">वर्ग</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">0-30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30-60</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">60-90</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">90-120</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">120-150</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">150-180</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">180-210</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">f</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">0</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">34</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">100</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">85</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">0</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">cf</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">0</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">34</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">134</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">219</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">249</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">271</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">271</td></tr></table>N = 271 → \\(\\frac{N}{2} = 135.5\\) → माध्यिका वर्ग 90–120 (l = 90, cf = 134, f = 85, h = 30)<br>माध्यिका = \\(90 + \\frac{135.5 - 134}{85} \\times 30 = 90 + 0.53 \\approx \\boxed{90.5}\\) मिनट<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 90.5 मिनट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q68.jpg"]}},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000075249","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A sum of money amounts to ₹11,616 at the end of 2 years and to ₹14,055.36 at the end of 4 years at compound interest, compounded annually. Find the rate of interest per annum and the original principal amount. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज (वार्षिक संयोजित) पर एक धनराशि 2 वर्ष के अंत में ₹11,616 और 4 वर्ष के अंत में ₹14,055.36 हो जाती है। प्रति वर्ष ब्याज दर और मूल मूलधन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Principal = ₹9,200<br>Annual Rate of Interest = 9%","hi":"मूलधन = ₹9,200<br>वार्षिक ब्याज दर = 9%"},"2":{"en":"Principal = ₹8,600<br>Annual Rate of Interest = 8%","hi":"मूलधन = ₹8,600<br>वार्षिक ब्याज दर = 8%"},"3":{"en":"Principal = ₹8,000<br>Annual Rate of Interest = 7%","hi":"मूलधन = ₹8,000<br>वार्षिक ब्याज दर = 7%"},"4":{"en":"Principal = ₹9,600<br>Annual Rate of Interest = 10%","hi":"मूलधन = ₹9,600<br>वार्षिक ब्याज दर = 10%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right)^2 = \\frac{14055.36}{11616} = 1.21 \\Rightarrow r = 10\\%\\)<br>\\(P = \\frac{11616}{1.21} = 9600\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{P = 9600,\\ r = 10\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Principal = ₹9,600<br>Annual Rate of Interest = 10%.</b>","hi":"\\(\\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right)^2 = \\frac{14055.36}{11616} = 1.21 \\Rightarrow r = 10\\%\\)<br>\\(P = \\frac{11616}{1.21} = 9600\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{P = 9600,\\ r = 10\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): मूलधन = ₹9,600<br>वार्षिक ब्याज दर = 10% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000075250","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"The square of a positive number exceeds the number itself by 182. Find the number. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक धनात्मक संख्या का वर्ग उस संख्या से 182 अधिक है। संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12"},"2":{"en":"13"},"3":{"en":"14"},"4":{"en":"15"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(x^2 - x = 182 \\Rightarrow x(x - 1) = 182 = 14 \\times 13\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{14}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 14.</b>","hi":"\\(x^2 - x = 182 \\Rightarrow x(x - 1) = 182 = 14 \\times 13\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{14}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 14 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000075251","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"The total manufacturing cost of an item is distributed among the factors - material sourcing, assembly labor and plant overheads - in the ratio 4:3:2. Due to shifting economic factors, material costs increase by 10%, assembly labor costs jump by 20% but plant overheads are successfully reduced by 5%. If these combined changes result in a net increase of Rs. 180 in the final manufacturing cost, find the initial total cost of manufacturing. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी वस्तु की कुल विनिर्माण लागत तीन घटकों - सामग्री, असेंबली श्रम और संयंत्र ओवरहेड - में 4:3:2 के अनुपात में बँटी है। बदलते आर्थिक कारकों के कारण, सामग्री लागत 10% बढ़ जाती है, असेंबली श्रम लागत 20% बढ़ जाती है, लेकिन संयंत्र ओवरहेड 5% कम हो जाते हैं। यदि इन संयुक्त परिवर्तनों से अंतिम विनिर्माण लागत में Rs. 180 की शुद्ध वृद्धि होती है, तो प्रारंभिक कुल विनिर्माण लागत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rs. 3600"},"2":{"en":"Rs. 2700"},"3":{"en":"Rs. 1800"},"4":{"en":"Rs. 900"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Costs = 4k, 3k, 2k (total 9k)<br>Net change = \\(0.4k + 0.6k - 0.1k = 0.9k = 180 \\Rightarrow k = 200\\)<br>Initial cost = \\(9 \\times 200 = \\boxed{1800}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Rs. 1800.</b>","hi":"लागतें = 4k, 3k, 2k (कुल 9k)<br>शुद्ध परिवर्तन = \\(0.4k + 0.6k - 0.1k = 0.9k = 180 \\Rightarrow k = 200\\)<br>प्रारंभिक लागत = \\(9 \\times 200 = \\boxed{1800}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): Rs. 1800 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000075252","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In an equilateral triangle ABC, the altitudes AD, BE, and CF intersect at point H. Find the ratio AH : HD. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक समबाहु त्रिभुज ABC में, शीर्षलंब AD, BE और CF बिंदु H पर प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं। अनुपात AH : HD ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 : 1"},"2":{"en":"2 : 1"},"3":{"en":"3 : 1"},"4":{"en":"3 : 2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"248\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 248 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M124 26L26 196L222 196ZM124 26L124 196M26 196L173 111M222 196L75 111M130 196L130 190L124 190\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"139\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"124\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"207\">C</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"207\">D</text><text x=\"181\" y=\"112\">E</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"112\">F</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"141\" text-anchor=\"start\">H</text></g></svg><br>In an equilateral triangle the altitudes are also medians<br>So the orthocentre H is the centroid, which divides each median in 2 : 1<br>AH : HD = \\(\\boxed{2 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2 : 1.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"248\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 248 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M124 26L26 196L222 196ZM124 26L124 196M26 196L173 111M222 196L75 111M130 196L130 190L124 190\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"139\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"124\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"207\">C</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"207\">D</text><text x=\"181\" y=\"112\">E</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"112\">F</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"141\" text-anchor=\"start\">H</text></g></svg><br>समबाहु त्रिभुज में शीर्षलंब ही माध्यिकाएँ भी होते हैं<br>अतः लंबकेंद्र H ही केन्द्रक है, जो प्रत्येक माध्यिका को 2 : 1 में बाँटता है<br>AH : HD = \\(\\boxed{2 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 : 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000075253","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}}\\), then find the value of \\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(x = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}}\\) है, तो \\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"42"},"3":{"en":"98"},"4":{"en":"83"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(x = (\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2})^2 = 5 + 2\\sqrt{6},\\ \\frac{1}{x} = 5 - 2\\sqrt{6}\\)<br>\\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 10\\)<br>\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 10^2 - 2 = \\boxed{98}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 98.</b>","hi":"\\(x = (\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2})^2 = 5 + 2\\sqrt{6},\\ \\frac{1}{x} = 5 - 2\\sqrt{6}\\)<br>\\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 10\\)<br>\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 10^2 - 2 = \\boxed{98}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 98 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000075254","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"A regional network operator measures the data recovery success speed of two distinct server nodes (Node A and Node B) across four testing scenarios. The findings are given in the following bar-graph:<br>Find the absolute numerical difference between the maximum recovery speed recorded by Node A and the minimum recovery speed recorded by Node B, and also that between the minimum recovery speed recorded by Node A and the maximum recovery speed recorded by Node B, respectively.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q74.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक क्षेत्रीय नेटवर्क ऑपरेटर चार परीक्षण परिदृश्यों में दो अलग-अलग सर्वर नोड्स (नोड A और नोड B) की डेटा रिकवरी गति मापता है। निष्कर्ष निम्नलिखित दंड आलेख में दिए गए हैं:<br>नोड A द्वारा दर्ज अधिकतम रिकवरी गति और नोड B द्वारा दर्ज न्यूनतम रिकवरी गति के बीच का निरपेक्ष संख्यात्मक अंतर, तथा नोड A द्वारा दर्ज न्यूनतम रिकवरी गति और नोड B द्वारा दर्ज अधिकतम रिकवरी गति के बीच का अंतर, क्रमशः ज्ञात कीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q74.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"35 terabytes/hr, 25 terabytes/hr"},"2":{"en":"25 terabytes/hr, 35 terabytes/hr"},"3":{"en":"35 terabytes/hr, 30 terabytes/hr"},"4":{"en":"30 terabytes/hr, 30 terabytes/hr"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Node A: 40, 55, 30, 65 → max 65, min 30<br>Node B: 35, 60, 45, 50 → max 60, min 35<br>|65 − 35| = 30; |30 − 60| = 30<br>\\(\\boxed{30,\\ 30}\\) terabytes/hr<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 30 terabytes/hr, 30 terabytes/hr.</b>","hi":"नोड A: 40, 55, 30, 65 → अधिकतम 65, न्यूनतम 30<br>नोड B: 35, 60, 45, 50 → अधिकतम 60, न्यूनतम 35<br>|65 − 35| = 30; |30 − 60| = 30<br>\\(\\boxed{30,\\ 30}\\) terabytes/hr<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 30 terabytes/hr, 30 terabytes/hr है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q74.jpg"]}},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000075255","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"For \\(a = 2, b = 3\\) and \\(c = 5\\), evaluate: \\((a + b + c)^3 - (a + b - c)^3 - (a - b + c)^3 - (-a + b + c)^3\\). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\\(a = 2, b = 3\\) और \\(c = 5\\) के लिए, मान ज्ञात कीजिए: \\((a + b + c)^3 - (a + b - c)^3 - (a - b + c)^3 - (-a + b + c)^3\\)। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"600"},"2":{"en":"660"},"3":{"en":"720"},"4":{"en":"780"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"a + b + c = 10, a + b − c = 0, a − b + c = 4, −a + b + c = 6<br>Value = \\(10^3 - 0^3 - 4^3 - 6^3 = 1000 - 0 - 64 - 216\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{720}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 720.</b>","hi":"a + b + c = 10, a + b − c = 0, a − b + c = 4, −a + b + c = 6<br>मान = \\(10^3 - 0^3 - 4^3 - 6^3 = 1000 - 0 - 64 - 216\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{720}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 720 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000075256","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the wrongly spelt word out of the four alternatives. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Millennium"},"2":{"en":"Perrenial"},"3":{"en":"Centennial"},"4":{"en":"Biannual"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Perennial (बारंबार) = lasting or recurring over a long time.</b><br><b>Perrenial</b> wrongly doubles “r”; the correct form is “perennial.”<br><b>Millennium (सहस्राब्दी)</b> = a thousand years; spelling correct.<br><b>Centennial (शताब्दी)</b> = a hundredth anniversary; <b>biannual (अर्धवार्षिक)</b> = twice yearly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Perrenial.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000075257","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the wrongly spelt word out of the four alternatives. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Pterodactyl"},"2":{"en":"Phsychology"},"3":{"en":"Pneumatic"},"4":{"en":"Pseudo"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Psychology (मनोविज्ञान) = the scientific study of mind and behaviour.</b><br><b>Phsychology</b> wrongly inserts “h” after the initial “p”; the correct spelling is “psychology.”<br><b>Pterodactyl (टेरोडैक्टिल)</b> = an extinct flying reptile; spelling correct.<br><b>Pneumatic (वायवीय)</b> = air-operated; <b>pseudo (छद्म)</b> = false.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Phsychology.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000075258","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.<br>The witness gave a <u>precise</u> account of the incident. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Specific"},"2":{"en":"Exact"},"3":{"en":"Inaccurate"},"4":{"en":"Correct"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Precise (यथार्थ) = exact and accurate.</b><br><b>Specific (विशिष्ट)</b> = clearly identified<br><b>Exact (यथार्थ)</b> = strictly correct<br><b>Inaccurate (अशुद्ध)</b> = containing errors ✔<br><b>Correct (सही)</b> = free from error<br>More antonyms: imprecise, vague, approximate.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Inaccurate.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000075259","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.<br>He is merely a <u>dilettante</u> who paints for fun but lacks any formal training. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Amateur"},"2":{"en":"Dabbler"},"3":{"en":"Professional"},"4":{"en":"Tyro"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Dilettante (शौकिया) = a person who pursues an art without serious professional commitment.</b><br><b>Amateur (शौकिया)</b> = non-professional<br><b>Dabbler (शौक में लिप्त)</b> = someone with superficial interest<br><b>Professional (व्यावसायिक)</b> = trained and engaged professionally ✔<br><b>Tyro (नौसिखिया)</b> = beginner<br>More antonyms: expert, specialist, master.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Professional.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000075260","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the correctly spelt word to replace the highlighted word in the given sentence.<br>He faced a <b>conundrom</b> regarding his future. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Conundrom"},"2":{"en":"Conundrum"},"3":{"en":"Connundrum"},"4":{"en":"Conunderum"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Conundrum (पहेली, दुविधा) = a confusing and difficult problem.</b><br>The correct spelling ends in “-drum.”<br><b>Conundrom</b> replaces “u” with “o”; <b>Connundrum</b> doubles “n.”<br><b>Conunderum</b> wrongly inserts “e.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Conundrum.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000075261","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the correctly spelt word to replace the highlighted word in the given sentence.<br>Her <b>supersilious</b> manner often alienated her from her many colleagues. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Superciliouss"},"2":{"en":"Supersilious"},"3":{"en":"Supercillious"},"4":{"en":"Supercilious"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Supercilious (अहंकारी) = behaving as though superior to others.</b><br>The correct spelling is “supercilious,” with “c” and one final “s.”<br><b>Superciliouss</b> doubles the final “s”; <b>Supersilious</b> uses “s” instead of “c.”<br><b>Supercillious</b> doubles “l.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Supercilious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000075262","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate option to fill the blank in the given sentence.<br>Tomorrow, I ___ the dusty old book from the attic and relive my favorite childhood memories. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Would open"},"2":{"en":"am open"},"3":{"en":"will open"},"4":{"en":"opened"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Tomorrow” requires a future form for the intended action.</b><br>“Will open” expresses the planned future action and parallels “relive.”<br>“Would open” is conditional, “am open” describes a state, and “opened” is past.<br>Only “will open” fits the time reference.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): will open.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000075263","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate option to fill the blank in the given sentence.<br>I managed to find my way to the museum only ___ a tattered paper map and a few landmarks. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"beneath"},"2":{"en":"by means of"},"3":{"en":"following the path"},"4":{"en":"barring"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>By means of (के माध्यम से) = using something as a method.</b><br>The traveller used a tattered map and landmarks to find the museum.<br>“Beneath” indicates position, “following the path” does not fit the map phrase, and “barring” means except.<br>Only “by means of” expresses the method.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): by means of.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000075264","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Pick out the homonym from the given options that can suitably complete both Sentence (P) and Sentence (Q) given below.<br>(P) Avian zoologists monitored the artificial environment, meticulously regulating thermal variables and humidity levels to ensure optimal embryonic development within the clutch.<br>(Q) Epidemiologists warned that the pathogenic agent possessed an extended, asymptomatic period, allowing infected hosts to propagate the virus across borders before clinical detection. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"expectancy"},"2":{"en":"dormancy"},"3":{"en":"incubation"},"4":{"en":"maturation"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Incubation (अंडे सेने की अवधि; रोग-उद्भव-पूर्व अवधि)</b><br>It describes both the development of embryos in eggs and the period before disease symptoms appear.<br>Expectancy means anticipation, dormancy means inactivity, and maturation means ripening.<br>Only “incubation” fits both scientific contexts.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): incubation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000075265","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the option in which the underlined homonym “assimilation” is used with the same meaning as in the sentence below.<br>The educational psychologist explained that cognitive schema expansion requires a careful balance between the assimilation of familiar data points and the accommodation of radically disruptive new concepts. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sociologists argue that forced cultural assimilation policies systematically erode indigenous languages and traditions, causing generational trauma by severing a community's connection to its heritage."},"2":{"en":"Gastroenterologists noted that structural damage to the intestinal villi severely compromises the metabolic assimilation of essential lipids, leading to systemic malnutrition despite adequate caloric intake."},"3":{"en":"Piagetian developmental theorists observe that a child utilises assimilation when they categorise a newly encountered target object, like a raccoon, into their pre-existing mental framework for “dogs.”"},"4":{"en":"Phonetic analysis reveals that rapid, colloquial speech frequently triggers mutual assimilation, where adjacent articulation points overlap and blend to minimise the mechanical effort required by the human vocal tract."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Cognitive assimilation = fitting new information into an existing mental schema.</b><br>Option C uses exactly this Piagetian sense: a child classifies a raccoon within an existing “dog” framework.<br>A concerns cultural absorption, B nutrient absorption, and D phonetic change.<br>Only C matches the educational-psychology meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Piagetian developmental theorists observe that a child utilises assimilation when they categorise a newly encountered target object, like a raccoon, into their pre-existing mental framework for “dogs.”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000075266","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the option that best explains the meaning of the underlined idiom in the sentence below.<br>In order to expedite the approval of the offshore drilling permits through the highly bureaucratic ministry, the multinational energy corporation resorted to <u>greasing the regional director's palm</u>. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Offering illicit financial inducements or surreptitious capital transfers to secure preferential treatment from an official"},"2":{"en":"Registering a systemic administrative grievance to censure an official for requlatory negligence"},"3":{"en":"Leveraging executive political networks to exert coercive, top-down institutional pressure on someone"},"4":{"en":"Utilising aggressive intimidation tactics to psychologically coerce someone into compliance"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Grease someone’s palm (रिश्वत देना) = bribe someone for preferential treatment.</b><br>The corporation illicitly induced the director to speed up the permit process.<br>Example: “The contractor greased the inspector’s palm.”<br>A grievance, political pressure and intimidation do not specifically express bribery.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Offering illicit financial inducements or surreptitious capital transfers to secure preferential treatment from an official.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000075267","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Read the sentences provided in options A, B, C, and D carefully. While three of the sentences are grammatically sound, one contains an “article usage” error. Identify the option with the error. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A trireme was a highly manoeuvrable ancient warship powered by the three rows of oars, designed by Mediterranean civilisations."},"2":{"en":"Following the catastrophic volcanic eruption on the island, the displaced were immediately provided with temporary shelter."},"3":{"en":"Mangroves protect vulnerable coastlines from severe tidal erosion by trapping sediment within their complex, intertwined root structures."},"4":{"en":"The blue whale is considered the largest animal ever known to have lived on Earth, occupying an apex position within marine ecosystems."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Do not use “the” before a simple numerical description unless the items are specifically identified.</b><br>Option A should read “powered by <b>three rows of oars</b>,” not “the three rows.”<br>“The displaced” correctly means displaced people in B.<br>C and D use their articles appropriately.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): A trireme was a highly manoeuvrable ancient warship powered by the three rows of oars, designed by Mediterranean civilisations.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000075268","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Read the sentences provided in options A, B, C, and D carefully. While three of the sentences are grammatically sound, one contains an “article usage” error. Identify the option with the error. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The telescope detected so distant a galaxy that its cosmic light took over thirteen billion years to reach the observatory's deep-space sensors."},"2":{"en":"The gallery curator remarked that it was quite masterpiece, possessing such a luminous quality that onlookers were instantly captivated."},"3":{"en":"What an extraordinary performance the understudy delivered tonight, stepping into the lead role with such absolute composure!"},"4":{"en":"What fascinating behavioural adaptations deep-sea organisms display when surviving under extreme hydrostatic pressure!"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Quite” precedes the indefinite article in “quite a + singular noun.”</b><br>Option B should read “it was <b>quite a masterpiece</b>.”<br>“So distant a galaxy” is correct in A, and “What an extraordinary performance” is correct in C.<br>D correctly uses the plural noun without an article.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The gallery curator remarked that it was quite masterpiece, possessing such a luminous quality that onlookers were instantly captivated.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000075269","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the following passive sentence into active voice. Then, select the correct option that maintains tense consistency and proper syntax.<br>A deep state of intimidation is easily experienced by them under a powerful leader, yet their assigned responsibilities are abandoned at that leader’s command, proving how quickly accountability is crushed by the leader. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They easily experience a deep state of intimidation under a powerful leader, yet they abandon their assigned responsibilities at that leader’s command, proving how quickly the leader crushes accountability."},"2":{"en":"They easily experienced a deep state of intimidation under a powerful leader, yet they abandon their assigned responsibilities at that leader's command, proving how quickly the leader crushes accountability."},"3":{"en":"They easily experienced a deep state of intimidation under a powerful leader, yet they abandoned their assigned responsibilities at that leader’s command, proving how quickly the leader crushes accountability."},"4":{"en":"They easily experience a deep state of intimidation under a powerful leader, yet they abandoned their assigned responsibilities at that leader’s command, proving how quickly the leader crushed accountability."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The passive agents become active subjects, and simple present remains simple present.</b><br>“Is experienced,” “are abandoned” and “is crushed” become “experience,” “abandon” and “crushes.”<br>B and C unnecessarily shift to past tense; D mixes present and past.<br>A preserves tense consistency throughout.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): They easily experience a deep state of intimidation under a powerful leader, yet they abandon their assigned responsibilities at that leader’s command, proving how quickly the leader crushes accountability.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000075270","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Read the sentence thoroughly, with special attention to the underlined segment. Choose the most appropriate substitution from A, B, or C. If the sentence is fine as it is, select D (No improvement required).<br>The micro-lending firm's public evaluation <u>would have read far more unfavourably than it did</u> if only the oversight committee had discovered the algorithmic bias earlier. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"would be read far more unfavourably than they did"},"2":{"en":"Would have read far more unfavourably than it done"},"3":{"en":"would read far more unfavourably than it had did"},"4":{"en":"No improvement required"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>The original conditional structure is correct.</b><br>“Would have read” gives the unreal past result, while “than it did” correctly refers to the actual evaluation.<br>A changes tense and pronoun number; B uses the nonstandard “it done.”<br>C incorrectly combines “had” with “did.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): No improvement required.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000075271","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Read the sentence thoroughly, with special attention to the underlined segment. Choose the most appropriate substitution from A, B, or C. If the sentence is fine as it is, select D (No improvement required).<br>The experimental composer conducted the discordant symphony <u>not because he lacked an understanding of classical harmony, but because he believed that traditional methods were obsolete</u>. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"not because he was lacking of an understanding in classical harmony, but because he had believed"},"2":{"en":"because he lacked an understanding of classical harmony, but because he has believed"},"3":{"en":"not lacking an understanding of classical harmony, but because he have believed"},"4":{"en":"No improvement required"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>The original sentence correctly uses parallel “not because … but because …” clauses.</b><br>“Lacked” and “believed” maintain past-tense consistency.<br>A uses “lacking of,” B drops “not” and changes tense, and C uses “have” with “he.”<br>No improvement is required.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): No improvement required.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000075272","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"The following sentence has been divided into four parts (P, Q, R, and S). The last part (S5) is fixed. Rearrange the remaining parts to form a grammatically correct and meaningful sentence, and choose the correct sequence.<br>P: especially as we ascend the scale and discover that certain animals are capable of remembering other animals<br>Q: the recognition of enemies can be noticed in animals quite low in the scale of life, and although this<br>R: after a hostile encounter with them, as shown quite plainly by the white mouse, that he had not forgotten the pet crow<br>S: psychical phase is almost universally instinctive, it carries with it certain elements of consciousness<br>S5: from whose clutches he had been rescued, even after three years had passed by. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RQSP"},"2":{"en":"QSPR"},"3":{"en":"PSQR"},"4":{"en":"SQRP"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QSPR</b><br>Q introduces recognition of enemies, and S completes “although this psychical phase ….”<br>P adds evidence of memory in higher animals.<br>R supplies the white-mouse example and leads into the fixed S5.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): QSPR.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000075273","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Select the correct passive form of the given sentence.<br>The police let the suspect go after questioning him for two hours. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The suspect was let to go by the police after being questioned for two hours."},"2":{"en":"The suspect was allow to go by the police after being questioned for two hours."},"3":{"en":"The suspect was let go by the police after being questioned for two hours."},"4":{"en":"The suspect was being let go by the police after being questioned for two hours."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Let + object + base verb” can become “object + be let + base verb.”</b><br>The participle “let” remains unchanged, and “go” stays without “to.”<br>A incorrectly inserts “to”; B uses “allow” instead of “allowed.”<br>D changes to continuous passive unnecessarily.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The suspect was let go by the police after being questioned for two hours.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000075274","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"In the following question, the first and last parts of a sentence are fixed as S1 and S5. The remaining parts, P, Q, R, and S, are given in jumbled order. Rearrange these parts to form a grammatically correct and logically meaningful sentence. Choose the correct sequence from the given options.<br>S1: It is possible that Claude Mollet, who began his career under Henri III<br>P: and wrote his elaborate work “Theatre des Plans et Jardinage” in 1612, which<br>Q: was only published half a century later, was the creator of the parterres and broderies<br>R: and plant forms resembling oriental embroideries in design, while making equal use of the labyrinth<br>S: so largely used in his time and after because his formula was derived chiefly from flower<br>S5: and the sunken garden, with the idea to develop the simple parquet into the elaborate parterre. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QSRP"},"2":{"en":"SPQR"},"3":{"en":"PQSR"},"4":{"en":"RSPQ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: PQSR</b><br>P continues Mollet’s career and introduces his book; Q completes the delayed-publication clause.<br>S begins explaining the source of his formula in flower forms.<br>R continues with plant forms and leads into the labyrinth and sunken garden in S5.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): PQSR.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000075275","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Select the correct passive form of the given sentence.<br>The research scholars would rather present their findings at the national seminar than publish them in a journal. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The findings would rather be presented at the national seminar then published in a journal by the research scholars."},"2":{"en":"The findings would rather be presented at the national seminar than be published in a journal by the research scholars."},"3":{"en":"The findings would rather have been presented at the national seminar than published in a journal by the research scholars."},"4":{"en":"The findings should rather be presented at the national seminar than published in a journal by the research scholars."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Would rather + base verb” becomes “would rather be + past participle.”</b><br>Parallel preference requires “than be published,” not “then.”<br>A confuses “then” with “than”; C adds an unnecessary perfect form.<br>D changes “would” to “should.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The findings would rather be presented at the national seminar than be published in a journal by the research scholars.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000075276","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by selecting the most appropriate option for each blank.<br><br>Climate policy is often presented as a contest between economic development and environmental restraint. This framing is misleading because unchecked warming itself threatens productivity, infrastructure, food security, and fiscal stability. (A)___, decarbonisation should be understood not as an impediment to economic progress but as a means of protecting its long-term foundations. The apparent conflict between growth and climate action arises largely from the unequal distribution of transitional costs.<br><br>Governments frequently hesitate to regulate carbon-intensive industries because such measures may provoke resistance from affected workers, businesses, and consumers. Yet postponement does not eliminate the burden; it merely (B)___ it, often transferring greater costs to younger generations and economically vulnerable communities. Had major economies begun restructuring their energy systems when scientific evidence became sufficiently clear, they (C)___ less exposed today to volatile fuel prices and climate-related disruption.<br><br>A credible transition therefore requires not only technological innovation but also a (D)___ that compensates affected workers, ensures transparent consultation, and distributes public investment fairly. Without such safeguards, climate policy may appear detached from the circumstances of communities least able to absorb sudden economic changes. Political leaders must therefore reckon (E)___ the social repercussions of reform rather than assuming that scientific urgency alone will secure public consent.<br><br><br>Choose the most appropriate option to fill in Blank (A). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nevertheless"},"2":{"en":"In other words"},"3":{"en":"Meanwhile"},"4":{"en":"By comparison"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>In other words (अर्थात) restates the preceding idea more clearly.</b><br>The passage reframes decarbonisation as protection of long-term economic foundations.<br>“Nevertheless” signals contrast, “meanwhile” signals simultaneity, and “by comparison” introduces comparison.<br>Only “in other words” fits the explanatory transition.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): In other words.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000075277","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by selecting the most appropriate option for each blank.<br><br>Climate policy is often presented as a contest between economic development and environmental restraint. This framing is misleading because unchecked warming itself threatens productivity, infrastructure, food security, and fiscal stability. (A)___, decarbonisation should be understood not as an impediment to economic progress but as a means of protecting its long-term foundations. The apparent conflict between growth and climate action arises largely from the unequal distribution of transitional costs.<br><br>Governments frequently hesitate to regulate carbon-intensive industries because such measures may provoke resistance from affected workers, businesses, and consumers. Yet postponement does not eliminate the burden; it merely (B)___ it, often transferring greater costs to younger generations and economically vulnerable communities. Had major economies begun restructuring their energy systems when scientific evidence became sufficiently clear, they (C)___ less exposed today to volatile fuel prices and climate-related disruption.<br><br>A credible transition therefore requires not only technological innovation but also a (D)___ that compensates affected workers, ensures transparent consultation, and distributes public investment fairly. Without such safeguards, climate policy may appear detached from the circumstances of communities least able to absorb sudden economic changes. Political leaders must therefore reckon (E)___ the social repercussions of reform rather than assuming that scientific urgency alone will secure public consent.<br><br><br>Choose the most appropriate option to fill in Blank (B). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"defers"},"2":{"en":"disperses"},"3":{"en":"diminishes"},"4":{"en":"disclaims"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Defer (स्थगित करना) = postpone or delay.</b><br>Postponement merely defers the burden and shifts greater costs to future generations.<br><b>Disperse (बिखेरना)</b> = scatter<br><b>Diminish (घटाना)</b> = reduce; <b>disclaim (अस्वीकार करना)</b> = deny responsibility<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): defers.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000075278","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by selecting the most appropriate option for each blank.<br><br>Climate policy is often presented as a contest between economic development and environmental restraint. This framing is misleading because unchecked warming itself threatens productivity, infrastructure, food security, and fiscal stability. (A)___, decarbonisation should be understood not as an impediment to economic progress but as a means of protecting its long-term foundations. The apparent conflict between growth and climate action arises largely from the unequal distribution of transitional costs.<br><br>Governments frequently hesitate to regulate carbon-intensive industries because such measures may provoke resistance from affected workers, businesses, and consumers. Yet postponement does not eliminate the burden; it merely (B)___ it, often transferring greater costs to younger generations and economically vulnerable communities. Had major economies begun restructuring their energy systems when scientific evidence became sufficiently clear, they (C)___ less exposed today to volatile fuel prices and climate-related disruption.<br><br>A credible transition therefore requires not only technological innovation but also a (D)___ that compensates affected workers, ensures transparent consultation, and distributes public investment fairly. Without such safeguards, climate policy may appear detached from the circumstances of communities least able to absorb sudden economic changes. Political leaders must therefore reckon (E)___ the social repercussions of reform rather than assuming that scientific urgency alone will secure public consent.<br><br><br>Choose the most appropriate option to fill in Blank (C). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Would have been"},"2":{"en":"were"},"3":{"en":"had been"},"4":{"en":"would be"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An unreal past condition with a present result uses “would + base verb.”</b><br>“Had major economies begun …, they <b>would be</b> less exposed today.”<br>“Today” makes the result present rather than a completed past outcome.<br>“Would have been” would refer to a past result; “were” and “had been” do not fit the conditional result.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): would be.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000075279","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by selecting the most appropriate option for each blank.<br><br>Climate policy is often presented as a contest between economic development and environmental restraint. This framing is misleading because unchecked warming itself threatens productivity, infrastructure, food security, and fiscal stability. (A)___, decarbonisation should be understood not as an impediment to economic progress but as a means of protecting its long-term foundations. The apparent conflict between growth and climate action arises largely from the unequal distribution of transitional costs.<br><br>Governments frequently hesitate to regulate carbon-intensive industries because such measures may provoke resistance from affected workers, businesses, and consumers. Yet postponement does not eliminate the burden; it merely (B)___ it, often transferring greater costs to younger generations and economically vulnerable communities. Had major economies begun restructuring their energy systems when scientific evidence became sufficiently clear, they (C)___ less exposed today to volatile fuel prices and climate-related disruption.<br><br>A credible transition therefore requires not only technological innovation but also a (D)___ that compensates affected workers, ensures transparent consultation, and distributes public investment fairly. Without such safeguards, climate policy may appear detached from the circumstances of communities least able to absorb sudden economic changes. Political leaders must therefore reckon (E)___ the social repercussions of reform rather than assuming that scientific urgency alone will secure public consent.<br><br><br>Choose the most appropriate option to fill in Blank (D). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"distributive framework"},"2":{"en":"Procedural formality"},"3":{"en":"rhetorical convention"},"4":{"en":"speculative arrangement"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Distributive framework (वितरणात्मक ढाँचा) = a system for fair allocation of costs and benefits.</b><br>It compensates workers and distributes public investment fairly.<br>A procedural formality is merely symbolic, a rhetorical convention concerns language, and a speculative arrangement lacks credibility.<br>Only a distributive framework addresses justice.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): distributive framework.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000075280","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by selecting the most appropriate option for each blank.<br><br>Climate policy is often presented as a contest between economic development and environmental restraint. This framing is misleading because unchecked warming itself threatens productivity, infrastructure, food security, and fiscal stability. (A)___, decarbonisation should be understood not as an impediment to economic progress but as a means of protecting its long-term foundations. The apparent conflict between growth and climate action arises largely from the unequal distribution of transitional costs.<br><br>Governments frequently hesitate to regulate carbon-intensive industries because such measures may provoke resistance from affected workers, businesses, and consumers. Yet postponement does not eliminate the burden; it merely (B)___ it, often transferring greater costs to younger generations and economically vulnerable communities. Had major economies begun restructuring their energy systems when scientific evidence became sufficiently clear, they (C)___ less exposed today to volatile fuel prices and climate-related disruption.<br><br>A credible transition therefore requires not only technological innovation but also a (D)___ that compensates affected workers, ensures transparent consultation, and distributes public investment fairly. Without such safeguards, climate policy may appear detached from the circumstances of communities least able to absorb sudden economic changes. Political leaders must therefore reckon (E)___ the social repercussions of reform rather than assuming that scientific urgency alone will secure public consent.<br><br><br>Choose the most appropriate option to fill in Blank (E). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"for"},"2":{"en":"upon"},"3":{"en":"with"},"4":{"en":"against"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Reckon with” means take something into account or confront its consequences.</b><br>Leaders must reckon with the social repercussions of reform.<br>“Reckon for” and “reckon against” are not standard here.<br>“Reckon upon” can mean rely on, which does not fit the intended meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): with.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};